{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.preludes.md | sed -n '228,500p'\"","aggregated_output":"   228\t### 4.5 `yrt.gen` and `yrt.safepoint` *(Tier-2 shared components, Slice P4)*\n   229\t\n   230\tDeferred to Slice P4 (after core + math lands) to bound P1 migration scope:\n   231\t- **`yrt.gen` (`py`, `php`, future `js`):** Extracts the `%capture` coroutine suspension/resume state machine (`gen-switch`, `gen-enter`, `yield-raw`).\n   232\t  - **Context policy difference (`py` vs. `php`):** In live code, `py/gen-enter` (`yang.python.antlr.prelude:457–458`) and `py/gen-start` (`:470`) compute a rebased `:base = (+ 1 (abs-depth caller-ctx))`, whereas `php/gen-start` (`yang.php.antlr.prelude:5311`) starts at `(php/ctx nil 0 0 nil)` and `php/gen-enter` (`:5305`) restores `(get s :ctx)` directly without rebasing. `yrt.gen` therefore accepts explicit `on-start-ctx` and `on-resume-ctx` policy closures alongside `on-enter`, `on-exit`, `on-fail`, and `on-throw-closed`, keeping PHP's refcount/cleanup lifecycle (`cleanup`, `addref`/`release`) and Python's `RecursionError` admission checks strictly language-owned.\n   233\t- **`yrt.safepoint` (`pysp`, `jssp`):** Extracts `stream/cursor`, `stream/poll!` gap/signal detection, and `attach!` setup into a shared module (`yrt.safepoint`), leaving signal delivery policy (`KeyboardInterrupt` / registered signal handler in `pysp`; uncatchable root `Interrupt` unwind in `jssp`) and recursion depth counting (`pysp`) in each hook module.\n   234\t\n   235\t---\n   236\t\n   237\t## 5. Declarative prelude composition, recipes, and admission\n   238\t\n   239\tTo eliminate ad-hoc `module-spec` and `admit` boilerplate while keeping every runtime dependency completely reproducible and content-pinned, **build-time emission recipes** and **immutable deployment profiles** are separated cleanly.\n   240\t\n   241\t### 5.1 Emission recipe vs. resolved runtime profile\n   242\t\n   243\t1. **`:yang.prelude/recipe` (host-side compiler recipe that *emits* a runtime module):**\n   244\t   Used by `yang.core.prelude` + `yang.core.prelude-admission` to produce the module's UAST, schema-1 manifest, and C1 side table from the owning language's definition list.\n   245\t   ```clojure\n   246\t   {:yang.prelude/schema 1\n   247\t    :yang.prelude/id :yang.python/py-prelude\n   248\t    :yang.prelude/revision \"2026-11-20.1\"\n   249\t    :yang.prelude/module 'py\n   250\t    :yang.prelude/components\n   251\t    [[yang.call \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   252\t     [yrt.escape \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   253\t     [yrt.float \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   254\t     [yrt.int \"<blake3-address>\"]]\n   255\t    :yang.prelude/host-modules\n   256\t    {:cell {:required true}\n   257\t     :data {:required true, :min-max-items 1048576}\n   258\t     :integer {:required true, :min-bits 53}}\n   259\t    :yang.prelude/emitter\n   260\t    {:mode :linear                 ;; :linear (definitions->uast) | :balanced (balanced-definitions->uast)\n   261\t     :uninit :py/uninit\n   262\t     :rt-namespaces #{\"py.rt\" \"py.b\"}\n   263\t     :unshadow-locals? false\n   264\t     :finalize-c1? true            ;; annotate :yang/call-site per current module emitter\n   265\t     :capture-safe-primitives nil} ;; optional for bundled clj mode\n   266\t    :yang.prelude/max-effects nil  ;; optional effect-ceiling set; nil = derive without extra ceiling\n   267\t    :yang.prelude/refusal-ns \"yang.python.antlr\"}\n   268\t   ```\n   269\t2. **`:yang.prelude/profile` (immutable, content-addressed runtime profile after publication):**\n   270\t   Replaces the recipe's local build knobs with the **published content address of the owning runtime module itself** (`:yang.prelude/root-address`) alongside the pinned transitive closure:\n   271\t   ```clojure\n   272\t   {:yang.prelude/schema 1\n   273\t    :yang.prelude/id :yang.python/py-prelude\n   274\t    :yang.prelude/revision \"2026-11-20.1\"\n   275\t    :yang.prelude/module 'py\n   276\t    :yang.prelude/root-address \"<blake3-address-of-published-py-module>\"\n   277\t    :yang.prelude/components\n   278\t    [[yang.call \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   279\t     [yrt.escape \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   280\t     [yrt.float \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   281\t     [yrt.int \"<blake3-address>\"]]\n   282\t    :yang.prelude/host-modules\n   283\t    {:cell {:required true}\n   284\t     :data {:required true, :min-max-items 1048576}\n   285\t     :integer {:required true, :min-bits 53}}\n   286\t    :yang.prelude/max-effects nil} ;; optional allowed-effect ceiling (e.g., the verified Python closure's #{:cell/new :cell/get :cell/set! :cell/authentic? :cell/new-provenance :cell/provenance}); nil = derive from verified closure without an extra ceiling\n   287\t   ```\n   288\t   A `:yang.prelude/profile` contains zero host functions or closures and passes `yang.frontend/non-portable-path`. Its `:yang.prelude/root-address` ensures two profiles cannot claim identical identity while pointing at different owning prelude definitions.\n   289\t\n   290\t### 5.2 Composition rules and verified-closure admission\n   291\t\n   292\t`yang.core.prelude` and `yang.core.prelude-admission` enforce six fail-closed checks:\n   293\t\n   294\t1. **Verified artifact closure input (`validate-profile`):**\n   295\t   - Admission takes `(profile artifact-store registry)`, where `artifact-store` supplies an **immutable, verified map `{address -> verified-manifest}`** (never assuming a graph from bare `[sym addr]` pairs!).\n   296\t   - Separately checks **direct root pins** and the **transitive closure**:\n   297\t     - Every `[sym addr]` in `:yang.prelude/components` and `:yang.prelude/root-address` resolves in `artifact-store`, and the root manifest's direct `:requires` map matches `:yang.prelude/components` (pinning direct edges without requiring transitive-only dependencies such as `clj.bridge` via `clojure.core` to be duplicated at the root).\n   298\t     - Recursively walks every `:requires` edge starting from `:yang.prelude/root-address` across `artifact-store`, verifying that every transitively reachable address resolves, that the full transitive `:requires` DAG is finite and acyclic, and that no two distinct addresses bind the same linker module symbol anywhere in the closure.\n   299\t2. **Export collision rule (qualified vs. projected):**\n   300\t   - Distinct Layer-2a/2b modules **may** share identical bare local export names (for instance, `yrt.float/abs` and `py/abs` coexist safely across qualified module borders).\n   301\t   - Collisions **are refused** whenever two components bind the same linker module symbol, when a local `module-definitions` key collides after namespace stripping, or when two source-facing `:ambient-projections` claim the same target identifier (`§6.3`).\n   302\t3. **Provenance-door security exclusion:**\n   303\t   - Validation verifies that no `yrt.*`, `clj.py`, or Layer-2c (e.g., `clojure.core`) manifest in the closure exports any `dsg__*` symbol or declares `:cell/new-provenance` or `:cell/provenance` in its derived effects.\n   304\t4. **Effect-ceiling verification (`:yang.prelude/max-effects`):**\n   305\t   - Rather than duplicating the manifest's derived effect set (honoring \"Derive, don't persist\"), `:yang.prelude/max-effects` is strictly optional. When present, admission checks `(clojure.set/subset? derived-transitive-effects max-effects)` and refuses if any transitive module or host declaration exceeds the ceiling.\n   306\t5. **Host-module and limit admission (`admit-profile`):**\n   307\t   - Because `yin.vm.module/register-host-module` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:249`) stores exports and profiles without retaining raw limit declarations (`yin.vm.integer` does not export `integer/max-bits`, and `yang.python.antlr.prelude/register-integer-module:4163` validates an explicit `limits` map before registration), **`admit-profile` takes `(profile artifact-store registry host-limits)`**.\n   308\t   - Verifies that `registry` supplies every required host export (`prelude-admission/admit`) AND verifies every declared floor in `:yang.prelude/host-modules` (`:min-bits`, `:min-digits`, `:min-max-items`) against the trusted composition `host-limits` map (failing closed if `host-limits` is absent or below the required floor, and cross-checking `integer/max-digits` / `data/max-items` against `host-limits` when present).\n   309\t6. **Dual-emitter preservation & Parity Law:**\n   310\t   - **Linked emission:** derives `:requires` and `:skip?` from `:yang.prelude/components`, emits `require` nodes in declared order, preserves `:rt-namespaces`, runs optional local unshadowing (`php`), and preserves exact C1 finalization (`:finalize-c1?` — matching `py`, `js`, `clj`, `yang.call` today while keeping `php` consistent).\n   311\t   - **Bundled emission (`compose-bundled`):** preserves existing ordering, `init!` placement, tail-marking, `:mode` (`:linear` vs `:balanced`, never silently altered because tree shape is content-addressed), and Clojure's custom preamble / `dsg__*` wrapper.\n   312\t   - **Bundled vs. Linked Parity Law:** Any program compiled under a composed prelude MUST produce identical outcomes in bundled and linked modes across the semantic, stack, and register VMs (and the AST walker once L-b lands).\n   313\t\n   314\t---\n   315\t\n   316\t## 6. Preludes as swappable libraries: the semantics descriptor contract\n   317\t\n   318\tMaking Layer-2a components reusable solves code duplication; making **Layer-2b/2c preludes swappable libraries** solves syntax-to-runtime coupling. A frontend like `yang.python` can then treat its runtime prelude as a pluggable library (`:yang.semantics/descriptor`).\n   319\t\n   320\t### 6.1 Level 1 vs. Level 2 library composition\n   321\t\n   322\t- **Level 1 — Ambient Library Projection:** Keep the frontend's native semantics (`py`, `js`, `php`) and link an external module (such as `clojure.core`) into its ambient lookup scope via `yang.call`.\n   323\t- **Level 2 — Pluggable Semantics Library:** Replace the frontend's lowering contract itself with a compatible prelude library (e.g., compiling Python syntax against `clojure.core` + `clj` directly onto persistent Yin data structures with zero value wrapping or marshalling).\n   324\t\n   325\tLevel 2 strictly subsumes Level 1: a semantics descriptor defines **both** what lowering emits for syntax constructs (`:yang.semantics/hooks` + `:yang.semantics/literals`) and which ambient modules/identifiers enter source scope (`:yang.semantics/ambient-modules` + `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections`).\n   326\t\n   327\t### 6.2 Core vs. Frontend ownership boundary\n   328\t\n   329\tTo preserve `yang.antlr.md` §3 (\"Yang core contains no enumeration of supported languages\"):\n   330\t- **`yang.core.semantics` (language-agnostic)** owns ONLY:\n   331\t  1. Generic schema validation for `:yang.semantics/descriptor`.\n   332\t  2. Pure, closed literal-strategy emission (`:raw`, `:float64-raw`, `:tagged-map`, `:raw-or-call`).\n   333\t  3. Generic capability lookup, hook-hygiene validation (every hook must be namespace-qualified), exact export verification against the descriptor's **selected, address-verified closure** across **every** executable descriptor field (hooks, executable literal strategies such as `:literals.*.overflow-op`, and ambient projections), and reserved-door projection checks.\n   334\t- **Each frontend package (e.g. `yang.python.antlr.contract`)** owns:\n   335\t  1. Its **fixed Hook ABI table** (`{hook-key {:arity n :required-by [...]}}`) specifying exact parameter conventions and structural lowering shapes for that frontend's grammar.\n   336\t  2. Structural AST lowering rules (e.g., how Python functions, loops, comprehensions, module packets, and `try`/`except`/`else`/`finally` marshal operands to those hooks).\n   337\t\n   338\t`yang.core.semantics` validates a descriptor **against the frontend-supplied contract table** — core never hardcodes Python, JS, or PHP syntax constructs.\n   339\t\n   340\t### 6.3 Portable `:yang.semantics/descriptor` schema\n   341\t\n   342\tA semantics descriptor contains **only portable data** (satisfies `yang.frontend/non-portable-path`):\n   343\t\n   344\t```clojure\n   345\t{:yang.semantics/schema 1\n   346\t :yang.semantics/id :yang.python/clojure-core-v1\n   347\t :yang.semantics/syntax :python\n   348\t :yang.semantics/prelude-module 'clj.py\n   349\t :yang.semantics/ambient-modules\n   350\t [{:module 'yang.call,     :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   351\t  {:module 'yrt.escape,    :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   352\t  {:module 'yrt.float,     :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   353\t  {:module 'yrt.int,       :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   354\t  {:module 'clj,           :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   355\t  {:module 'clj.bridge,    :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   356\t  {:module 'clojure.core,  :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   357\t  {:module 'clj.py,        :address \"<blake3-address>\"}]\n   358\t\n   359\t :yang.semantics/capabilities\n   360\t {:mutation/locals      :cell          ;; :cell | :single-assignment | :refused\n   361\t  :mutation/subscript   :refused       ;; :supported | :refused\n   362\t  :mutation/attribute   :refused\n   363\t  :mutation/delete      :refused\n   364\t  :scope/global         :supported     ;; per-module globals cell only\n   365\t  :scope/nonlocal       :supported     ;; lexical cells when :mutation/locals is :cell\n   366\t  :calls/positional     :supported\n   367\t  :calls/varargs        :supported     ;; *args\n   368\t  :calls/defaults       :refused\n   369\t  :calls/kwonly         :refused\n   370\t  :calls/kwstar         :refused\n   371\t  :calls/kwargs         :refused\n   372\t  :destructuring/unpack :refused       ;; explicit choice; or :supported via clj.py/unpack\n   373\t  :expr/comprehensions  :supported     ;; eager list/set/dict only; genexpr gated by :control/generators\n   374\t  :control/exceptions   :supported     ;; bare `except:` + `finally` + `raise` (`except Exc as e:` requires :control/except-typed; `except as e:` is invalid Python 3 grammar)\n   375\t  :control/except-typed :refused       ;; class-matched / typed `except ExcType [as e]:` refused when :oo/classes :refused\n   376\t  :control/generators   :refused       ;; gates BOTH `yield`/`yield from` AND generator expressions\n   377\t  :control/with         :refused\n   378\t  :oo/classes           :refused\n   379\t  :modules/import       :ambient-only} ;; :supported | :ambient-only | :refused\n   380\t\n   381\t :yang.semantics/literals\n   382\t {:nil     {:kind :raw, :value nil}\n   383\t  :bool    {:kind :raw}\n   384\t  :str     {:kind :raw}\n   385\t  :float   {:kind :float64-raw}      ;; vs {:kind :tagged-map, :tag :py/float}\n   386\t  :int     {:kind :raw-or-call, :safe-max-bits 53, :overflow-op 'clj.py/int-lit}\n   387\t  :unbound {:kind :raw, :value :clj/unbound}}\n   388\t\n   389\t :yang.semantics/hooks\n   390\t {;; Arithmetic & comparisons — ALL namespace-qualified (hygienic, immune to guest shadowing)\n   391\t  :op/add           'clj.py/add\n   392\t  :op/sub           'clj.py/sub\n   393\t  :op/mul           'clj.py/mul\n   394\t  :op/truediv       'clj.py/truediv\n   395\t  :op/floordiv      'clj.py/floordiv\n   396\t  :op/mod           'clj.py/mod\n   397\t  :op/pow           'clj.py/pow\n   398\t  :op/neg           'clj.py/neg\n   399\t  :op/pos           'clj.py/pos\n   400\t  :op/eq            'clj.py/eq\n   401\t  :op/ne            'clj.py/ne\n   402\t  :op/lt            'clj.py/lt\n   403\t  :op/le            'clj.py/le\n   404\t  :op/gt            'clj.py/gt\n   405\t  :op/ge            'clj.py/ge\n   406\t  :op/lnot          'clj.py/lnot\n   407\t  :op/truthy        'clj.py/truthy\n   408\t  ;; Collections, indexing, and comprehension accumulators\n   409\t  :coll/vconj       'clj.py/vconj\n   410\t  :coll/list        'clj.py/list\n   411\t  :coll/tuple       'clj.py/tuple\n   412\t  :coll/set         'clj.py/set-from\n   413\t  :coll/dict        'clj.py/map-from\n   414\t  :coll/getitem     'clj.py/get-item\n   415\t  :comp/list-new    'clj.py/comp-list-new    ;; [init-vec] -> accumulator; py-v1: 'py/list\n   416\t  :comp/list-append 'clj.py/comp-list-append ;; [acc val] -> step result; py-v1: 'py/list-append\n   417\t  :comp/set-new     'clj.py/comp-set-new     ;; [] -> accumulator; py-v1: 'py/set-new\n   418\t  :comp/set-add     'clj.py/comp-set-add     ;; [acc val] -> step result; py-v1: 'py/set-add\n   419\t  :comp/dict-new    'clj.py/comp-dict-new    ;; [] -> accumulator; py-v1: 'py/dict-new\n   420\t  :comp/dict-set    'clj.py/comp-dict-set    ;; [acc k v] -> step result; py-v1: 'py/dict-set\n   421\t  :comp/finish      'clj.py/comp-finish      ;; optional [acc] -> final collection; nil in py-v1\n   422\t  ;; Scopes & bindings\n   423\t  :env/local-get    'clj.py/local-get\n   424\t  :env/global-get   'clj.py/global-get\n   425\t  :env/global-set   'clj.py/global-set\n   426\t  ;; Functions & calls\n   427\t  :fn/arg           'clj.py/arg\n   428\t  :fn/make          'clj.py/make-fn\n   429\t  :fn/call          'clj.py/call\n   430\t  ;; Control flow & unit entry\n   431\t  :ctrl/for-each    'clj.py/for-each\n   432\t  :ctrl/try         'clj.py/try\n   433\t  :ctrl/try-finally 'clj.py/try-finally\n   434\t  :ctrl/raise       'clj.py/raise\n   435\t  :ctrl/call-ec     'clj.py/call-ec\n   436\t  :unit/run-main    'clj.py/run-main}\n   437\t\n   438\t ;; Each entry defaults to :kind :cell-accessor (resolves `(m/e)` to obtain the\n   439\t ;; module's stable task-local authenticated callable cell); optional :kind :value\n   440\t ;; reads an immutable non-callable export directly.\n   441\t :yang.semantics/ambient-projections\n   442\t {\"identity\"  {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'identity,  :kind :cell-accessor}\n   443\t  \"inc\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'inc,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n   444\t  \"dec\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'dec,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n   445\t  \"str\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'str,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n   446\t  \"count\"     {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'count,     :kind :cell-accessor}\n   447\t  \"first\"     {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'first,     :kind :cell-accessor}\n   448\t  \"rest\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'rest,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   449\t  \"second\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'second,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n   450\t  \"cons\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'cons,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   451\t  \"conj\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'conj,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   452\t  \"assoc\"     {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'assoc,     :kind :cell-accessor}\n   453\t  \"assoc_in\"  {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'assoc-in,  :kind :cell-accessor}\n   454\t  \"get\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'get,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n   455\t  \"get_in\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'get-in,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n   456\t  \"update\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'update,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n   457\t  \"update_in\" {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'update-in, :kind :cell-accessor}\n   458\t  \"map\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'map,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n   459\t  \"filter\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'filter,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n   460\t  \"reduce\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'reduce,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n   461\t  \"into\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'into,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   462\t  \"keys\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'keys,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   463\t  \"vals\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'vals,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   464\t  \"merge\"     {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'merge,     :kind :cell-accessor}\n   465\t  \"is_empty\"  {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'empty?,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n   466\t  \"is_nil\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'nil?,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   467\t  \"is_map\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'map?,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   468\t  \"is_vector\" {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'vector?,   :kind :cell-accessor}\n   469\t  \"is_set\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'set?,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   470\t  \"ex_info\"   {:module 'clj.py,       :export 'ex-info,   :kind :cell-accessor}}}\n   471\t```\n   472\t\n   473\t### 6.4 Validation, lexical hygiene, authority checks, and address neutrality\n   474\t\n   475\t1. **Hygienic generated references (no bare hook symbols):**\n   476\t   - Every symbol in `:yang.semantics/hooks` (when non-nil, e.g., optional `:comp/finish`) and every literal-strategy call symbol (such as `:literals.*.overflow-op`) **MUST be namespace-qualified** (e.g., `clj.py/vconj`, `py/vconj`, `clj.py/add`, `clj.py/int-lit`). Unqualified symbols (such as bare `conj`, `+`, `not`, `set`) are rejected at validation (`:yang.semantics/unqualified-hook`), because bare symbols inside lowered UAST could be silently captured by a valid Python parameter or local named `conj` or `not`.\n   477\t2. **Scope-aware precedence for `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections`:**\n   478\t   - Free source identifiers resolve in strict order:\n   479\t     1. **Lexical scope** (`:local`, `:cell`, `:nonlocal` parameter or local variable, including a local named `map` or `conj`),\n   480\t     2. **Per-module globals** (`globals` dictionary via `:env/global-get`, allowing module-level `def` or `global` assignment to shadow an ambient binding cleanly),\n   481\t     3. **`:yang.semantics/ambient-projections`** (resolved via `clj.py/global-get` fallback to the module's explicit projected lookup map, calling `(m/e)` for `:kind :cell-accessor` entries, or refused at runtime/admission if absent).\n   482\t   - Defining or binding a parameter named `conj` or `is_empty` shadows only that source lookup and **never** alters compiler-generated calls to `clj.py/vconj`, `clj.py/add`, etc.\n   483\t3. **Exact export & reserved-door authority validation against the selected closure (`validate-descriptor`):**\n   484\t   - Takes `(descriptor frontend-contract artifact-store registry)`:\n   485\t     - Computes the descriptor's **selected, address-verified closure**: every `[module address]` in `:yang.semantics/ambient-modules` must resolve in `artifact-store` along with its full transitive `:requires` DAG (with unique module-symbol bindings).\n   486\t     - Inspects **every executable reference anywhere in the descriptor**: every active hook in `:yang.semantics/hooks` (including non-nil optional hooks such as `:comp/finish`), every executable literal-strategy field (such as `:yang.semantics/literals.*.overflow-op`), and every `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` target (`{:module m :export e}`).\n   487\t     - Verifies every such symbol is namespace-qualified (for hooks and literal strategies), matches the frontend-authorized role and arity in `frontend-contract`, and exists as an **exact published export in the selected, address-verified closure** (or in a host module of `registry` explicitly required by that selected closure and permitted by `frontend-contract`, or an allowed non-reserved VM primitive). An export belonging to an unrelated manifest somewhere else in `artifact-store` outside the descriptor's selected closure is **rejected**!\n   488\t     - For `:ambient-projections`, checks unique source names and, when `:kind :cell-accessor` (the default), verifies that module `m` exports both the named 0-arg accessor `e` and its idempotent task table initializers (`init!`, `export`).\n   489\t     - **Reserved-door ban:** Refuses any descriptor whose `:hooks`, executable `:literals.*` fields, or `:ambient-projections` references `cell/dsg__*`, `dsg__*`, `yin/def`, `*.rt/*`, `*.b/*`, `yang.safepoint/*`, or non-projectable internal adapter entries (`clojure.core/raw-*`), or exposes any unprivileged raw primitive without projection. Registry availability never grants source-level authority.\n   490\t   - Any violation fails closed before reading CST packets with `:yang.semantics/invalid-descriptor`.\n   491\t4. **Fail-closed capability enforcement during lowering:**\n   492\t   - Before lowering any guarded CST construct (e.g., `classdef`, `yield_expr`, `genexpr`, `with_stmt`, `del_stmt`, typed `except E:` / `except E as e:`, keyword argument call, default parameter value, subscript assignment), the lowering checks the descriptor's capability map.\n   493\t   - Generator expressions MUST check `:control/generators` (so they cannot evade generator refusal even when `:expr/comprehensions` is `:supported`).\n   494\t   - Any disabled/absent capability emits:\n   495\t     ```clojure\n   496\t     {:status :refused\n   497\t      :reason :yang.semantics/unsupported-capability\n   498\t      :capability :oo/classes\n   499\t      :semantics-id :yang.python/clojure-core-v1\n   500\t      :construct \"classdef\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.preludes.md | sed -n '501,662p'\"","aggregated_output":"   501\t      :node <cst-node-id>}\n   502\t     ```\n   503\t5. **Byte-identical default-profile invariant (`P2`, zero golden churn for decoupling):**\n   504\t   - Refactoring `yang.python.antlr.lower` (in **Slice P2** — and subsequently TypeScript/PHP) to read from `:yang.semantics/descriptor` MUST emit **byte-identical UAST rows** under the default descriptor (`:yang.python/py-v1`, carrying all `py/*` hooks including `:comp/list-new 'py/list`, `:comp/list-append 'py/list-append`, `:comp/set-new 'py/set-new`, `:comp/set-add 'py/set-add`, `:comp/dict-new 'py/dict-new`, `:comp/dict-set 'py/dict-set`, `:comp/finish nil`, `{:kind :tagged-map, :tag :py/float}`, `{:kind :tagged-map, :tag :py/str}`, `:py/None`, and existing supported capabilities) compared to the pre-refactor hardcoded lowering. Zero existing golden addresses move in P2.\n   505\t\n   506\t### 6.5 Frontend SPI and provenance integration (`yang.frontend`)\n   507\t\n   508\tNo `yang.frontend` schema change is required (`src/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc`):\n   509\t- `:yang.frontend/id` continues to name the frontend syntax + lowering implementation (e.g., `:yang.python/antlr`), and each distinct configuration receives a distinct immutable `:yang.frontend/revision` (e.g., `\"py-v1\"` vs. `\"clojure-core-v1\"` — re-installing `[id revision]` with a different manifest returns `:yang.frontend/revision-conflict`).\n   510\t- `:yang.frontend/lowering-profile` pins the content address of the `:yang.semantics/descriptor` EDN artifact.\n   511\t- `:yang.frontend/runtime-profile` pins the content address of the resolved `:yang.prelude/profile` manifest.\n   512\t- Compilation provenance records `(cst-address, lowering-profile, runtime-profile, unit-address)` as data; note that distinct descriptors may legitimately yield identical UAST addresses on simple programs (many-to-one), so provenance retains the exact compilation tuple rather than inferring the descriptor from the UAST address alone.\n   513\t\n   514\t---\n   515\t\n   516\t## 7. Case study: `yang.python` with a `clojure.core` prelude (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`)\n   517\t\n   518\tThis section specifies the reference cross-paradigm profile in full, reconciling Python's lowering ABI, 4-host numeric portability, cross-unit callable admission, §8.10.7 exception bridging, and a portable `clojure.core` module.\n   519\t\n   520\t### 7.1 Value representation & semantic mapping\n   521\t\n   522\t| Python syntax | Native `py` prelude (`:yang.python/py-v1`) | `clojure.core` prelude (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`) |\n   523\t|---|---|---|\n   524\t| `None` | `:py/None` | `nil` |\n   525\t| `True` / `False` | `true` / `false` (numeric as `1`/`0`) | `true` / `false` (**non-numeric**: arithmetic raises guest error) |\n   526\t| `\"abc\"` | `{:py/str \"abc\"}` | `\"abc\"` (raw Yin/UTF-8 string) |\n   527\t| `42` | exact integer (safe raw, else `py/int-lit`) | exact integer (safe raw, else `clj.py/int-lit`) |\n   528\t| `1.5` | `{:py/float <float64>}` | `<float64>` (untagged Jing `data/float64` carrier) |\n   529\t| `[1, 2]` | cell `{:py/type :list :items [1 2]}` | persistent vector `[1 2]` |\n   530\t| `(1, 2)` | `{:py/type :tuple :items [1 2]}` | persistent vector `[1 2]` |\n   531\t| `{\"a\": 1}` | cell `{:py/type :dict ...}` | persistent map `{\"a\" 1}` |\n   532\t| `{1, 2}` | cell `{:py/type :set ...}` | persistent set `#{1 2}` |\n   533\t| `def f(x): ...` | cell `{:py/type :function :code (fn [args] ...) :yang.call/entry ...}` | authenticated cell `{:clj.py/type :function :name s :spec spec :yang.call/entry ...}` |\n   534\t| Truthiness | `0`, `\"\"`, `[]`, `{}`, `None`, `False` falsy | Clojure truthiness (`clj.py/truthy`): only `nil` and `false` falsy (`0`, `\"\"`, `[]` are truthy) |\n   535\t| Equality `==` / `!=` | `1 == 1.0 == True`, structural list/dict | Recursive kind-strict equality (`clj.py/eq`): `1 == 1` `true`, `1 == 1.0` `false`, `1 == True` `false`, `NaN == NaN` `false`, `0.0 == -0.0` `true`, recursive over persistent collections |\n   536\t\n   537\t*Truth-in-advertising invariant:* `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` explicitly declares Clojure truthiness, persistent immutable collections, non-numeric booleans, and kind-strict equality as its support profile — never CPython parity.\n   538\t\n   539\t### 7.2 Portable numeric & collection contract (`clj.py` over `yin.vm.integer` + `yrt.float` + `yrt.int`)\n   540\t\n   541\tPer `yang.antlr.md` §8.5.5, raw `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=` on decoded `data/float64` carriers are **not portable across Node/JVM/Dart**. Furthermore, `yin.vm.data/data-number?` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc:418`) recognizes host numbers and exact-integer carriers, **not** CLJS `Float64` carriers (`src/cljc/dao/host/number.cljc:76`).\n   542\t\n   543\t**P3 Host prerequisites (`data/float64?` and `kind/namespace`):**\n   544\t1. **`data/float64?`** (`src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc`): one `:pure` unary export backed directly by existing `dao.jing.cbor/float64?` (`src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:212` — already implemented for JVM `Double`/`Float`, Dart `double`, JS `Float64`/non-integral/non-finite/`-0.0` `Number`, and Jolt Scheme flonums).\n   545\t2. **`kind/namespace`** (`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2578`, `:kind-module` / `:kind-arities`): one `:pure` unary export backed by `namespace`, enabling standalone `clojure.core` (`§7.5`) to sort and render namespaced symbols and keywords deterministically without host `kind/str`.\n   546\tLike owner decision A12.6 in `yang.typescript.md`, adding these two pure host exports changes no existing `py`/`js`/`php`/`clj` manifest or golden address; both are explicit prerequisites of P3 and are not needed in P1.\n   547\t\n   548\tTherefore, `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` routes ALL arithmetic, floor division, remainder, power, comparisons, and equality through `clj.py/*` adapters requiring host `integer` (`:min-bits 53`) and `data` (with `data/float64?`):\n   549\t\n   550\t1. **Portable kind classification (`clj.py/num-kind`):**\n   551\t   ```clojure\n   552\t   (if (integer/integer? x)\n   553\t     :int\n   554\t     (if (data/float64? x) :float :other))\n   555\t   ```\n   556\t   `true`/`false`, `nil`, strings, symbols, keywords, collections, callables, and cells all answer `:other` cleanly across all four hosts (`integer/integer?` at `src/cljc/yin/vm/integer.cljc:595`). Non-numeric operands raise guest error `{:clj.py/error :type-error ...}` (in `v1`, string `+` concatenates via `data/str-concat`; `*` is strictly numeric).\n   557\t2. **Int × Int (universal `yrt.int/check-limit` gate):**\n   558\t   - **Every** `integer/*` operation returning through `yin.vm.integer`'s `out` / `pair` contract (`add`, `sub`, `neg`, `mul`, `floor-div-mod`, `quot-rem`, `pow`, `to-float`, `true-div`, `from-float`, `format` — including **`integer/neg`** on externally supplied exact operands!) MUST pass through `yrt.int/check-limit` **before** indexing a `[q r]` pair via `data/nth` or forwarding a result into any subsequent `integer/*` or `yrt.float/*` primitive. Any `:yin.vm.integer/bit-limit`, `:digit-limit`, or `:float-overflow` reason translates to a guest error map via `clj/raise`; operational host throws are never caught.\n   559\t   - `+`, `-`, `*`, `//`, `%`, `**` (`e >= 0`), `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`: check `b == 0` **before** `integer/floor-div-mod` or `integer/true-div` (raising guest zero-division error rather than an operational throw); filter `floor-div-mod` through `yrt.int/check-limit` before calling `data/nth` for `//` or `%`.\n   560\t   - `/`: checks `b != 0`, calls `(yrt.int/check-limit (integer/true-div a b) ...)`, and boxes via `data/float64`.\n   561\t   - `**` with negative integer exponent `e < 0`: if `a == 0` raises guest zero-division error; otherwise computes `base-boxed = (data/float64 (yrt.int/check-limit (integer/to-float a) ...))` and `pos-e = (yrt.int/check-limit (integer/neg e) ...)`, and calls `(yrt.float/neg-pow-result base-boxed pos-e :half)`. If `yrt.float/neg-pow-result` returns `:yrt.float/underflow`, `clj.py` raises guest overflow error `{:clj.py/error :overflow ...}` outside any raw-double leaf frame.\n   562\t   - Unary `-` (`clj.py/neg`) / `+` (`clj.py/pos`): unary `-` computes `(yrt.int/check-limit (integer/neg a) ...)`; unary `+` returns `a` unchanged.\n   563\t3. **Float × Float and Mixed Int × Float:**\n   564\t   - Exact int operands promote via `(data/float64 (yrt.int/check-limit (integer/to-float i) ...))`.\n   565\t   - **`+`, `-`, `*`:** Unwrap both boxed floats via `data/float-value` inside pure leaf helpers, evaluate IEEE-754 double `+`, `-`, `*`, and rebox via `data/float64` (producing IEEE `±Inf`/`NaN` on overflow/invalid results).\n   566\t   - **`/` (`clj.py/truediv`):** Unwraps boxed `y` in a pure leaf helper to check `(yrt.float/zero? y)` **first** and raises guest zero-division error `{:clj.py/error :zero-division :op :truediv}` (consistent with Int × Int `/`, `//`, and `%`); for nonzero `y`, delegates boxed operands to `yrt.float/fdiv` (returning boxed `data/float64`, including IEEE `±Inf`/`NaN` on `x = ±Inf` / `NaN` / finite overflow).\n   567\t   - **Unary `-` and `+` on `:float`:** Unary `-` unwraps `x` in a pure leaf helper and returns `(data/float64 (* (data/float-value -1) x))` (preserving signed zero `-0.0 ↔ +0.0` across CLJD/JVM/CLJS/Jolt, never `(- 0 x)`); unary `+` returns the boxed `data/float64` unchanged.\n   568\t   - **`//` (`clj.py/float-floordiv`):**\n   569\t     - Zero divisor (`y == 0.0`): raises guest zero-division error `{:clj.py/error :zero-division :op :floordiv}`.\n   570\t     - `NaN` in either operand, or non-finite `x` (`±Inf`): returns boxed `yrt.float/nan` (matching `py/float-divmod:1426`).\n   571\t     - Finite `x`, infinite `y` (`±Inf`): handled directly in a leaf helper — if `x == 0.0` returns `(data/float64 (* (data/float-value 0) (/ x y)))` (preserving signed zero); if `x != 0.0` and signs differ returns `(data/float64 -1)`, else `(data/float64 0)`.\n   572\t     - Finite `x`, finite nonzero `y`: inside pure leaf helper `clj.py/float-floordiv-raw [x y]`, mirrors `py/float-divmod` (`src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:1427–1437`):\n   573\t       - `m0 = (yrt.float/fmod-pos (yrt.float/abs x) (yrt.float/abs y))`, `m = (if (< x 0) (- 0 m0) m0)`\n   574\t       - `adjust = (if (yrt.float/zero? m) false (not (= (< y 0) (< m 0))))`\n   575\t       - `div = (- (/ (- x m) y) (data/float-value (if adjust 1 0)))`\n   576\t       - **Signed-zero quotient branch:** `(if (yrt.float/zero? div) (* (data/float-value 0) (/ x y)) ...)` — preserves `-0.0 // 2.0 -> -0.0` and `0.0 // -2.0 -> -0.0`.\n   577\t       - **Quotient rounding correction:** `(let [f (yrt.float/float-floor-raw div)] (if (< (data/float-value 0.5) (- div f)) (+ f (data/float-value 1)) f))` — ensures `2.1 // 0.7` (whose intermediate `div` is `2.9999999999999996`, flooring to `2.0`) evaluates to **`3.0`** while non-finite or `>= 2^53` quotients pass through unchanged; result is boxed via `data/float64`.\n   578\t   - **`%` (`clj.py/float-mod`):** guards ALL preconditions before ever reaching `yrt.float/fmod-pos`:\n   579\t     - Zero divisor (`y == 0.0`): raises guest zero-division error.\n   580\t     - `NaN` in either operand, or non-finite `x` (`±Inf`): returns boxed `yrt.float/nan`.\n   581\t     - Finite `x`, infinite `y` (`±Inf`): handled directly without `fmod-pos` — returns `zero-like(y)` when `x == 0.0`, `x` when `x` and `y` share sign, and `y` (`±Inf`) when signs oppose (floored modulo).\n   582\t     - Finite `x`, finite nonzero `y`: calls `m0 = (yrt.float/fmod-pos (abs x) (abs y))` inside a pure leaf frame, restores dividend sign `m`, converts `m == 0.0` to `zero-like(y)`, sign-corrects `m` toward `y`, and returns `data/float64`.\n   583\t   - **`**` (`clj.py/float-pow` — strict leaf unwrap + limit check before compare):**\n   584\t     - Pure leaf helper `clj.py/float-exp-info [y-boxed]` unwraps `y = (data/float-value y-boxed)` (so `yin.vm.integer/float!` receives a native unwrapped `host-float?` on all 4 hosts, including CLJS!):\n   585\t       - Returns `:zero` when `(yrt.float/zero? y)`, `:nan` when `(yrt.float/nan? y)`, `:infinite` when `(not (yrt.float/finite? y))`;\n   586\t       - Otherwise (finite nonzero `y`), binds `e = (integer/from-float y)` and **checks `(integer/integer? e)` BEFORE calling `(integer/compare-float e y)`**! If `e` is a limit keyword (e.g., `:yin.vm.integer/bit-limit` for `2.0 ** 53` at `:max-bits 53`), returns that keyword immediately out of the leaf frame (never passing `:yin.vm.integer/bit-limit` into `integer/compare-float`); otherwise checks `(= (integer/compare-float e y) 0)` and returns exact integer `e` or `:fractional`.\n   587\t     - Outer wrapper `clj.py/float-pow` (with no raw double live!) handles `:zero -> (data/float64 1)` (even for `NaN ** 0.0`), `:nan -> (yrt.float/nan)`, `:infinite -> guest :pow-infinite`, `:fractional -> guest :pow-fractional`, and translates limit reasons via `yrt.int/check-limit`.\n   588\t     - For exact integral `e`: checks `x` NaN via pure leaf unwrap (`-> (yrt.float/nan)`); for `e >= 0`, evaluates `yrt.float/fpow-half-raw` inside a pure leaf helper and boxes via `data/float64`; for `e < 0`, checks `x == 0.0` (`-> guest :zero-division`), computes `pos-e = (yrt.int/check-limit (integer/neg e) ...)`, and calls `(yrt.float/neg-pow-result x-boxed pos-e :half)` (translating `:yrt.float/underflow` to guest `:overflow` outside the leaf frame).\n   589\t   - **Mixed ordering (`<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`):** Float × Float unwraps both via `data/float-value` inside a pure leaf helper; Int × Float / Float × Int unwraps the boxed float via `data/float-value` inside a pure leaf helper, returns `false` if `(yrt.float/nan? f)`, and calls `integer/compare-float` strictly on the unwrapped non-NaN host double (never passing a boxed CLJS `Float64` or `NaN` to `integer/compare-float` and never rounding large integers to float).\n   590\t4. **Uniform portable key/element domain (`admit-key!`) & recursive equality (`clj.py/eq`, `clj.py/ne`):**\n   591\t   - **Why a uniform key/element gate is required (`yin/vm/data.cljc:34–36`, `dao.jing.cbor.md:173`):** Host map/set hashing and Jing canonical CBOR encoding cannot recover distinct keys (`1` vs `1.0`, `[[-0.0]]`, `NaN`) once collapsed by host collection construction, and host map/set lookup diverges across JVM (`1 != 1.0`) vs JS (`1 == 1.0`).\n   592\t   - **One uniform `v1` portable key/element admission gate (`admit-key!`):** Enforced across BOTH `clj.py` (`map-from`, `set-from`, `get-item`, `comp-set-add`, `comp-dict-set`) AND standalone `clojure.core` (`assoc`, `assoc-in`, `update`, `update-in`, `get`, `get-in`, `contains?`, `conj` on maps/sets, `disj`, `merge`, `into` when targeting maps/sets, `union`, `difference`, `hash-map`, `set`):\n   593\t     - **Admitted keys / set elements (recursively):** `nil`, booleans, exact integers (`integer/integer?`), strings, keywords, symbols, and persistent vectors, persistent maps (both keys and values checked recursively), and persistent sets recursively containing **only** admitted values.\n   594\t     - **Refused keys / set elements at ANY nesting depth:** any `data/float64?` value (`0.0`, `-0.0`, `1.0`, `NaN`, `±Inf`, or nested `[[-0.0]]`, `{\"a\" 1.0}`), lists/seqs (`seq?`, preventing Jing/host list-vs-vector collisions when used as map keys or set elements), host closures/continuations, and `:cell-ref` handles — raising guest error `{:clj.py/error :unsupported-key :key k}` (`ex-info` in `clojure.core`).\n   595\t     - Arbitrary floats (`-0.0`, `1.0`, `NaN`, `±Inf`), lists, and callables remain **fully supported as map values and vector/list elements**!\n   596\t     - Because every admitted key or set element is recursively float-free and list-free, host map/set construction, update, lookup, and membership agree 100% across JVM, CLJS/Node, CLJD/Dart, and Jolt with zero `1`/`1.0`, `0.0`/`-0.0`, `NaN`, or `[1]`/`'(1)` collapse.\n   597\t   - **Recursive portable equality (`clj.py/eq`, `clj.py/ne`):** Never delegates floats or float-bearing values to host `=`, because CLJS `Float64.-equiv` (`src/cljc/dao/host/number.cljc:98–101`) equates `NaN` with `NaN` and distinguishes `-0.0` from `0.0`:\n   598\t     - `:int` × `:int`: `(= (integer/compare a b) 0)`.\n   599\t     - `:float` × `:float`: leaf unwrap → `false` if either is NaN, else `(= ax bx)` (`+0.0 == -0.0` is `true`, `NaN == NaN` is `false` on all 4 hosts).\n   600\t     - `:int` × `:float` (or vice versa): **`false`** (kind-strict Clojure equality: `1 != 1.0`).\n   601\t     - Vectors / sequential collections (`data/vector?`, `clojure.core/sequential?`): equal count + pairwise recursive `clj.py/eq`.\n   602\t     - Maps (`data/map?`, excluding authenticated cell-refs): equal count + every key `k` present in both (exact admitted key match) with values recursively equal via `clj.py/eq` (falling back cleanly to recursive key/value pair scanning if an externally constructed map is ever passed) — so `{\"a\": -0.0} == {\"a\": 0.0}` is `true` and `{\"a\": NaN} == {\"a\": NaN}` is `false` on all 4 hosts.\n   603\t     - Sets (`kind/set?`): equal count + exact admitted membership across all elements (`#{}` with excluded float/list elements cannot arise inside `clj.py`/`clojure.core`).\n   604\t     - Other scalars (`nil`, booleans, strings, keywords, symbols, authenticated cell-refs): host `=`.\n   605\t\n   606\t### 7.3 Python lowering Hook ABI & `clj.py` adapters\n   607\t\n   608\tRather than pretending `clj/*` shares identical signatures with `py/*`, the frontend keeps its fixed **Python Lowering Hook ABI** (`yang.python.antlr.contract`) and `clj.py` implements every hook with compatible arity and semantics:\n   609\t\n   610\t| Hook key | Frontend ABI signature | `clj.py` implementation |\n   611\t|---|---|---|\n   612\t| `:env/local-get` | `[cell name]` | Reads `(cell/get cell)`; raises guest unbound error if `:clj/unbound` (supporting parameter init, local reassignment, and `nonlocal` via shared lexical cells when `:mutation/locals :cell`). |\n   613\t| `:env/global-get` | `[globals-cell name]` | Reads the unit's **per-module** `globals-cell` first; on miss, falls back to `clj.py`'s explicit `:ambient-projections` lookup table (invoking the 0-arg accessor `(m/e)` for `:kind :cell-accessor` entries to obtain the stable task-local authenticated callable cell); on miss there, raises guest `NameError`-equivalent map `{:clj.py/error :name-error :name name}`. Keeps distinct compiled modules isolated instead of sharing one flat `clj.rt/globals` map. |\n   614\t| `:env/global-set` | `[globals-cell name value]` | Writes `(cell/set! globals-cell (assoc (cell/get globals-cell) name value))` and returns `value`. |\n   615\t| `:fn/make` | `[fname spec defaults kwdefaults code]` | Accepts the exact 5 arguments from `yang.python.antlr.lower/function-value:1870` (lowering already refused defaults/kwonly/kwstar/kwargs when disabled); delegates to trusted Layer-2b **`clj.bridge/make-callable`** (`§7.4`) allocating an authenticated task-heap cell. |\n   616\t| `:fn/call` | `[callee args]` | Delegates directly to trusted Layer-2b **`clj.bridge/invoke-callable`** (`§7.4`), which checks `clj.bridge/admitted-callable?` first and routes to `yang.call/invoke` with the condition-unwrapping / provenance-retaining raise exit. Zero provenance doors inside `clj.py`. |\n   617\t| `:ctrl/try` | `[body handler orelse]` | **3-arg signature** calling `yrt.escape/try-orelse` on `(clj/rt-ctx)` (sharing Clojure's exception domain by design), preserving Python `try` / `except` / `else`. |\n   618\t| `:ctrl/try-finally` | `[body fin]` | Calls `yrt.escape/try-finally` on `(clj/rt-ctx)` with `normal-arg = nil`. |\n   619\t| `:ctrl/raise` | `[e]` | Calls `clj/raise` (delegating to `yrt.escape/raise` on `(clj/rt-ctx)`). |\n   620\t| `:ctrl/call-ec` | `[f]` | Calls `yrt.escape/call-ec` on `(clj/rt-ctx)` with `normal-arg = nil`. |\n   621\t| `:ctrl/for-each` | `[iterable step-fn]` | Invokes pinned pure adapter entry **`clojure.core/raw-seq`** (and `raw-first`/`raw-rest`, never calling a cell-valued 0-arg export accessor directly as a function!), iterates deterministic canonical `[k v]` pairs for maps and canonical elements for sets, raises guest error on non-collection iterables, and invokes `step-fn` per element (supports `break`/`continue` via `call-ec` and eager comprehensions). |\n   622\t| `:comp/list-new`, `:comp/set-new`, `:comp/dict-new` | `[init-vec]`, `[]`, `[]` | Allocates a temporary local accumulator cell holding persistent `[]`, `#{}`, or `{}` (`cell/new []`, `cell/new #{}`, `cell/new {}`). |\n   623\t| `:comp/list-append`, `:comp/set-add`, `:comp/dict-set` | `[acc val]`, `[acc val]`, `[acc k v]` | Reads `(cell/get acc)`, validates set elements / dict keys via `admit-key!`, updates via `(cell/set! acc (conj cur val))` / `(assoc cur k v)`, and returns `:py/None` (in `clj.py`, `nil`). |\n   624\t| `:comp/finish` | `[acc]` *(optional)* | Returns `(cell/get acc)` (the immutable persistent vector/set/map). Omitted (`nil`) in `:yang.python/py-v1` so default Python lowering stays byte-identical. |\n   625\t| `:unit/run-main` | `[body-fn]` | Calls idempotent `(clj/init!)`, `(clojure.core/init!)`, and `(clj.py/init!)`; allocates a **fresh per-unit `globals` cell** (`(cell/new {})`) and `globals-fn`; invokes `(body-fn globals globals-fn)` inside a top-level handler on `(clj/rt-ctx)`; returns the value **verbatim without stripping `[:yin.k/ok ...]`** so ordinary Python data shaped like `[:yin.k/ok 42]` passes through uncorrupted. |\n   626\t\n   627\t*(Lowerings with `:mutation/locals :single-assignment` remain a separate, stricter profile variant that omits local variable cells and refuses assignment/reassignment to locals, loops with mutated accumulators, and `nonlocal`.)*\n   628\t\n   629\t### 7.4 Trusted `clj.bridge`, cross-unit callable admission, and §8.10.7 validation\n   630\t\n   631\tBecause `yang.call/eligible?` (`src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc:29–48`) only dereferences authenticated cell-refs and leaves ordinary maps intact, structural eligibility alone does **not** stop source-constructed maps carrying `:yang.call/entry` from masquerading as callables when source maps are first-class data. Likewise, as `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1280–1306` and `2400–2424` show, immutable Clojure descriptors carry a unit-local `:clj/admission` witness closing over that unit's private `dsg__call_token` rather than cross-unit admission, whereas **authenticated task-heap cells** (`cell/authentic?`, `clojure.cljc:2400–2408`) are admitted across **every** independently compiled unit (`yang.clojure`, `clojure.core`, `clj.py`, `py`, `js`, `php`).\n   632\t\n   633\t**Trusted Layer-2b provenance boundary (`clj.bridge`):**\n   634\tAll Clojure-family §8.10.7 entry/call provenance bridging is consolidated into a **single stateless trusted Layer-2b module `clj.bridge`** (`src/cljc/yang/clojure/bridge.cljc`), requiring `yang.call`, `yrt.escape`, and `clj`.\n   635\t- `clj.bridge` owns the private provenance doors (`cell/dsg__new-provenance`, `cell/dsg__provenance`) inside **both** its linked (`module-uast`) and bundled (`uast`) emitters (preserving §5.2 Bundled vs. Linked Parity Law!), never exporting them and keeping them strictly out of `yrt.*`, `clj.py`, and Layer-2c `clojure.core`.\n   636\t- Operating directly on `(clj/rt-ctx)` alongside `clj`, `clj.py`, and `clojure.core` leaves existing `yang.clojure` / `clj` byte-identical in Slice P3.\n   637\t\n   638\t`clj.bridge` enforces the full §8.10 + §8.10.7 contract:\n   639\t\n   640\t1. **Source-level callable admission (`clj.bridge/admitted-callable?`):**\n   641\t   - Called by `clj.bridge/invoke-callable`, `clj.py/callable?`, `clojure.core/fn?`, and `clojure.core`'s dynamic higher-order caller **before** invoking `yang.call/invoke`. Written strictly in prelude special-form notation (`yang.core.uast/sexp->uast:82` — nested `if`, zero `and` form!):\n   642\t     ```clojure\n   643\t     (if (data/map? x)\n   644\t       (if (= (get x :type) :cell-ref)\n   645\t         (if (cell/authentic? x)\n   646\t           (if (data/callable? (yang.call/entry x))\n   647\t             (yang.call/eligible? x)\n   648\t             false)\n   649\t           false)\n   650\t         false)\n   651\t       false)\n   652\t     ```\n   653\t   - Any plain source map (including `{:yang.call/entry ...}`), unauthenticated `{:type :cell-ref ...}` map, or raw host primitive/continuation fails `admitted-callable?` cleanly; `invoke-callable` mints a retained `:yang.call/not-callable` protocol condition via private `cell/dsg__new-provenance` and raises it via `(clj/raise ...)`, never calling `yang.call/invoke` on forged source data.\n   654\t   - Preserves zero-wrapper function identity (`=`) across all cell-backed frontends (`py`, `js`, `php`, `clj.py`, standalone `clojure.core`). Note the explicit boundary: foreign immutable non-cell descriptors (such as legacy unit-local `yang.clojure` descriptors) are not admitted as raw maps in `clj.py` or standalone `clojure.core`, avoiding receiver-side replacement wrappers (`yang.antlr.md` §8.10.2).\n   655\t2. **Trusted cell-backed callable constructor (`clj.bridge/make-callable`):**\n   656\t   - Given descriptor metadata map `meta` and body/binder thunk `bind-and-run`, allocates an authenticated task-heap cell `(cell/new (assoc meta :yang.call/entry entry))` where `entry` closes over the owner cell `owner` and enforces Step 3 below.\n   657\t3. **Full 4-step invocation-record validation & §8.10.7 entry boundary (mirroring `py/function-entry:906–943`):**\n   658\t   - **Step A — Establish usable raise exit first:** verify `(data/map? invocation)` and `(data/callable? (get invocation :yang.call/raise))`. If missing or non-callable, fail operationally right away (never invoke an invalid exit or convert wiring corruption into a guest catchable error).\n   659\t   - **Step B — Validate protocol record & owner identity (outside `try-value`):** check `(yang.call/valid-invocation? invocation)` AND `(= (get invocation :yang.call/callee) owner)`. On failure, transfer `(yang.call/condition :yang.call/invalid-invocation {:yang.call/callee owner})` directly via `yang.call/transfer`.\n   660\t   - **Step C — Reject unsupported binding extensions (outside `try-value`):** if `(data/contains? invocation :yang.call/binding-profile)`, transfer `(yang.call/condition :yang.call/unsupported-binding {:yang.call/callee owner, :yang.call/binding-profile (get invocation :yang.call/binding-profile)})` directly via `yang.call/transfer`.\n   661\t   - **Step D — Value-returning boundary (`yrt.escape/try-value` — NOT `try-orelse`!) around binding + body:**\n   662\t     - Installs the exception handler on `(clj/rt-ctx)` **before** argument binding so ordinary named-arg / positional-arity errors share the same boundary (`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1244–1256` and `yang.antlr.md:3861–3867` §8.10.7): inside `try-value`, checks `:yang.call/named` and positional/varargs arity against `:spec` (raising local guest binding exceptions via `clj/raise` so they cross under **`:yang.call/thrown`**) and evaluates `(bind-and-run positional named)`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
