{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.preludes.md | sed -n '663,865p'\"","aggregated_output":"   663\t     - On normal completion, `yrt.escape/try-value` restores `(clj/rt-ctx)` and returns the body's value verbatim (`20` in §7.6).\n   664\t     - On escape with `e`, the handler inspects private `(cell/dsg__provenance e)`: if non-nil (an authentic retained protocol condition from a deeper cross-language boundary), forwards that retained condition **directly** to `raise-exit` without double-wrapping; otherwise wraps `e` (including condition-shaped user maps!) via `(yang.call/thrown e)` and transfers it to `raise-exit`.\n   665\t4. **Call-site boundary (`clj.bridge/invoke-callable`):**\n   666\t   - Validates `(clj.bridge/admitted-callable? callee)`; if false, mints private retained `:yang.call/not-callable` via `cell/dsg__new-provenance` and raises on `(clj/rt-ctx)`.\n   667\t   - Otherwise calls `yang.call/invoke` with a dedicated `raise-exit` closure:\n   668\t     - If `(= (get condition :yang.call/reason) :yang.call/thrown)`, calls `(clj/raise (get condition :yang.call/value))` (unwrapping user-thrown values identically to `clojure.cljc:1441–1447`).\n   669\t     - Otherwise retains the protocol condition inside a private provenance carrier `(clj/raise (cell/dsg__new-provenance condition condition))` (mirroring `clojure.cljc:1448–1450`), preserving full condition fidelity across `A → B → A` unwinds and `finally` blocks, as well as nested `clj → clj.py → clj` unwinding on `(clj/rt-ctx)`.\n   670\t\n   671\t### 7.5 Portable `clojure.core` linked library contract\n   672\t\n   673\tIn Slice P3, `clojure.core` is published as an **explicit, standalone, portable Layer-2c linker module** (`clojure.core`) requiring `yang.call`, `clj`, `clj.bridge`, `yrt.float`, and `yrt.int` (zero direct provenance doors!), and registered against host modules `kind` (with pure `kind/namespace`), `data` (with pure `data/float64?`), `integer` (`:min-bits 53`), and `cell` (strictly omitting host-dependent exports):\n   674\t\n   675\t1. **Audited observable operations — portable subset and adaptations (`yang.clojure/library` base + 4-host rewrites):**\n   676\t   - **Pure non-numeric definitions retained verbatim** (rewritten in prelude notation using nested `if`, zero `and`, and routing map/set traversals through canonical order where noted): `identity`, `second`, `boolean?`, `count`, `symbol?`, `keyword?`, `meta`, `name`, `symbol`, `keyword`, `last`, `butlast`, `string?`, `with-meta`, `coll?`, `vector?`, `set?`, `sequential?`, `seq?`, `list?`, `reverse`, `cons`, `list`, `vector`, `reduced`, `unreduced`, `concat`.\n   677\t   - **Explicit portable rewrites & exclusions (strictly inside standalone `clojure.core`, leaving default `yang.clojure` untouched):**\n   678\t     - `inc`, `dec`: route through portable numeric dispatch (`integer/integer?` → `integer/add`/`integer/sub` + `yrt.int/check-limit`; `data/float64?` → leaf unwrap ± `(data/float-value 1)` + `data/float64`; non-numeric → guest type error via `clj/raise`), never bare VM `+`/`-` (`yin.vm.cljc:404`).\n   679\t     - `rem`: validates `(if (integer/integer? a) (integer/integer? b) false)` and `b != 0` (raising guest errors otherwise), checks **`qr = (yrt.int/check-limit (integer/quot-rem a b) ...)` BEFORE calling `(data/nth qr 1)`** (so `:yin.vm.integer/bit-limit` never reaches `data/nth` as a keyword!), never catching host operational throws.\n   680\t     - `not=`: delegates to portable recursive equality (`§7.2`: exact `integer/compare`, unwrapped float `-0.0 == 0.0` / `NaN != NaN`, kind-strict `1 != 1.0`, recursive collection equality), never leaking CLJS `Float64.-equiv`.\n   681\t     - `int?`: delegates to `integer/integer?` (consistent exact-integer answer across all 4 hosts, including JS/Dart big integers).\n   682\t     - `fn?`: **identical to `clj.bridge/admitted-callable?`** (`nested if` checking `data/map?`, `:type = :cell-ref`, `cell/authentic?`, `data/callable? entry`, `yang.call/eligible?`). **No `(data/callable? x)` fallback**: `fn?` returns `false` for raw host primitives, continuations, and forged maps so `fn?` agrees 1-to-1 with what `clj.py/call` and `clojure.core`'s dynamic higher-order caller actually admit!\n   683\t     - `map?`, `reduced?`: exclude authenticated `:cell-ref` handles (`(if (= (get x :type) :cell-ref) (not (cell/authentic? x)) true)`) so function cells never report `map? -> true`.\n   684\t     - `fresh-symbol`, `gensym`: validate exact integer supply `:counter` via `integer/integer?`, increment strictly via **`integer/add` + `yrt.int/check-limit`**, format integers via **`integer/format` + `yrt.int/check-limit`**, and concatenate via `data/str-concat` (eliminating bare `(+ (:counter supply) 1)` and host `kind/str`).\n   685\t     - `str`: explicit 4-host deterministic renderer (never delegating arbitrary values to host `kind/str`!): `nil -> \"\"`; strings verbatim; booleans `\"true\"`/`\"false\"`; exact integers via `integer/format` + `yrt.int/check-limit`; `data/float64?` via pure leaf unwrap + `integer/float-digits` + `yrt.float` decimal layout (`zeros`/`exp-text`) with explicit `\"NaN\"`, `\"Infinity\"`, `\"-Infinity\"`, `\"0.0\"`, `\"-0.0\"` branches so `1.0` renders `\"1.0\"` (never JS `\"1\"`) across all 4 hosts; keywords (`\":\"`) & symbols via `kind/namespace` + `kind/name`; vectors/lists recursively; maps and sets in canonical key order (`canonical-compare`); authenticated callable cells as `\"#<fn>\"`.\n   686\t     - **Canonical map/set traversal (`canonical-compare`) — eliminating host iteration order:** Standalone `clojure.core` defines a deterministic total order over the admitted `v1` key/element domain (`§7.2`: type rank `nil < boolean < exact integer (integer/compare) < string (data/str-compare) < keyword (kind/namespace, kind/name via data/str-compare) < symbol < vector < map < set`). `raw-seq`, `seq`, `first`, `rest`, `vec`, `keys`, `vals`, `str`, `reduce`, `map`, `filter`, `remove`, `into`, `merge`, `union`, and `difference` all normalize map entry pairs `[k v]` and set elements into canonical sorted order before producing ordered sequences — guaranteeing identical `keys`, `vals`, `vec`, and `seq` results on JVM, CLJS/Node, CLJD/Dart, and Jolt.\n   687\t     - `nth`: validates index via `integer/integer?`, checks bounds via `integer/compare`, and restricts to sequential collections (`sequential?` or `vector?`, never indexing unordered maps/sets in host iteration order).\n   688\t     - **Uniform portable key/element gate (`admit-key!`):** `assoc`, `assoc-in`, `update`, `update-in`, `get`, `get-in`, `contains?`, `conj` (on maps and sets), `disj`, `merge`, `into` (targeting maps/sets), `union`, `difference`, `hash-map`, and `set` all enforce `admit-key!` (`§7.2`: recursively refusing any `data/float64?` or `seq?` key/element on all 4 hosts).\n   689\t   - **Explicitly excluded for 4-host portability:** `var?` (CLJ-only in `kind-module:2593`), `resolve` (`kind/resolve` absent from `kind-module`), and `yang.clojure`'s internal `invoke-value`.\n   690\t2. **Newly authored portable helpers & primitive callable projections (not pre-existing in `yang.clojure/library`):**\n   691\t   - Pure guest additions in `clojure.core`: `assoc-in`, `update-in`, `get-in`, `hash-map`, `set`.\n   692\t   - **Primitive callable projections:** thin cell-backed callable wrappers over VM primitives (`nil?`, `empty?`, `not`, `first`, `conj`, `assoc`, `get`, `vec`, enforcing `admit-key!` on `conj`/`assoc`/`get` for maps/sets) so Python source can either call `is_empty(xs)` directly OR pass `is_empty` as a higher-order callback to `filter`/`map`.\n   693\t3. **Linker-safe export table, idempotent `init!`, 0-arg cell accessors, and reconciled call path:**\n   694\t   - **Why linker snapshots cannot store task cells (`src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:915, 1055`, `yin/vm/module.cljc:40`):** `yin.vm.engine/lift-slice` snapshots module exports at install-child halt and refuses to lift `:cell-ref` values. Therefore `clojure.core` publishes **zero cells at install time**:\n   695\t     1. Internal non-exported runtime placeholders `clojure.core.rt/state` and `clojure.core.rt/exports` start at `:clojure.core/uninit`.\n   696\t     2. **`clojure.core/init!` (`[]`):** Idempotent per-task initializer — when `clojure.core.rt/state` is `:clojure.core/uninit`, ensures `(clj/init!)`, constructs ONE authenticated cell per public library function via `clj.bridge/make-callable` (each cell's `:yang.call/entry` dispatches to the module's stripped internal `raw-*` implementation lambda inside `clj.bridge`'s §8.10.7 boundary), stores the `{sym cell}` map via `(yin/def (quote clojure.core.rt/exports) (cell/new export-map))`, and flips `(yin/def (quote clojure.core.rt/state) :clojure.core/ready)`. Repeat calls in the same task are no-ops, returning `:clojure.core/ready` without mutating or regenerating cells.\n   697\t     3. **`clojure.core/export` (`[sym]`):** Calls `(clojure.core/init!)` and returns `(get (cell/get clojure.core.rt/exports) sym)` — the **stable task-local authenticated cell** for `sym`. Two importers in one Yin task receive the exact same (`=`) cell; two separate tasks receive isolated cells.\n   698\t     4. **Public 0-arg cell-accessor exports:** For every public library function `<name>` (including projected `empty?`, `nil?`, `map`, `filter`, `reduce`, etc.), `clojure.core` exports a pure cell-free lambda `(fn [] (clojure.core/export (quote <name>)))`. Because these exports are pure functions, `lift-slice` succeeds cleanly; `validate-descriptor` verifies every projected name directly against the published manifest; and callers (`clj.py`, `py`, `js`, `php`, bundled or linked) invoke `(clojure.core/<name>)` to retrieve the stable task-local cell and call it via `clj.bridge/invoke-callable` / `yang.call/invoke`.\n   699\t     5. **Separately named internal adapter entries (`raw-*`):** Pure implementation entries (`clojure.core/raw-seq`, `clojure.core/raw-first`, `clojure.core/raw-rest`) are exported strictly under the reserved `raw-*` internal adapter prefix (banned from `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` by `validate-descriptor`), allowing trusted Layer-2b hooks such as `clj.py/for-each` to iterate directly without going through a 0-arg cell accessor.\n   700\t   - **Dynamic closure construction & internal call discipline:**\n   701\t     - Every closure returned at runtime by `comp`, `partial`, or higher-order helpers is also constructed via `clj.bridge/make-callable` (producing an authenticated task-heap cell compatible across all units with preserved `=` identity and zero receiver-side wrappers).\n   702\t     - Static internal sibling calls within `clojure.core` invoke stripped internal `raw-*` implementation lambdas directly (zero allocation, immune to caller global redefinition).\n   703\t     - Dynamic calls to user-supplied callbacks (`f` in `map`, `filter`, `remove`, `reduce`, `update`, `update-in`, `comp`, `partial`) route exclusively through `clj.bridge/invoke-callable` — **never** using `yang.clojure`'s map-only `[dsg__call_token args]` shortcut (`clojure.cljc:2432`).\n   704\t4. **No implicit namespace dump & zero impact on default `yang.clojure` in P3:**\n   705\t   - Adding `'clojure.core` to `:requires` exposes nothing to user code on its own; only explicit entries in `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` enter source scope.\n   706\t   - Existing `yang.clojure`'s `library-for` bundling stays untouched in P3 so default Clojure compilation keeps zero golden churn; migrating `yang.clojure` itself onto `clojure.core` is scheduled separately (owner decision D6).\n   707\t\n   708\t### 7.6 Concrete lowering example\n   709\t\n   710\t```python\n   711\tdef sum_even_squares(xs):\n   712\t    if is_empty(xs):\n   713\t        return 0\n   714\t    evens = filter(lambda n: n % 2 == 0, xs)\n   715\t    squares = map(lambda n: n * n, evens)\n   716\t    return reduce(lambda a, b: a + b, 0, squares)\n   717\t```\n   718\t\n   719\t- `is_empty` resolves (below lexical/module scope) via `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` to `clojure.core`'s projected `empty?` cell-backed callable.\n   720\t- `filter`, `map`, `reduce` resolve to `clojure.core`'s task-instantiated cell-backed callables.\n   721\t- `%`, `*`, `+`, `==` lower hygienically to `clj.py/mod`, `clj.py/mul`, `clj.py/add`, `clj.py/eq` (exact `yin.vm.integer` / `yrt.float` paths).\n   722\t- `lambda n: ...` lowers to `clj.py/make-fn`, producing an authenticated cell-backed `yang.call` callable invoked directly by `clojure.core/filter` and `clojure.core/map`.\n   723\t- `sum_even_squares([1, 2, 3, 4])` evaluates `[1 2 3 4]` → `20` (exact persistent integer), and returns `20` unchanged (not unwrapped by `[:yin.k/ok ...]`).\n   724\t\n   725\t---\n   726\t\n   727\t## 8. Portability, content addressing, and malleability\n   728\t\n   729\t### 8.1 Multi-host portability (JVM, CLJS/Node, CLJD/Dart, Jolt/Scheme)\n   730\t\n   731\tAll new `yang.core.*` and `yang.rt.*` (`yrt.*`) namespaces live in `src/cljc/` and obey the repository's four-host constraints:\n   732\t- **ClojureDart AOT literal limits:** Consolidate `defquoted` (`yang.python.antlr.prelude`, `yang.typescript.antlr.prelude`, `yang.php.antlr.quoted`) into `yang.core.prelude/defquoted`, keeping identical `:cljs`/`:cljd` macro imports, reader aliases, and EDN expansion.\n   733\t- **No bare integral float literals & safe integer bounds:** `yrt.float` and `clj.py` construct every float constant via `data/float-value`/`data/float64`, `-0.0` via `(* (data/float-value -1) (data/float-value 0))`, and avoid integer literals past `2^53 - 1`.\n   734\t- **Canonical ordering (`b86bc0e8` invariant):** Recipes, profiles, descriptor maps, and emitted UAST operand sequences sort keys deterministically (`sort-by str` / explicit vector order) and never iterate host maps when building AST nodes, guaranteeing byte-identical `dao.jing.cbor` hashes across JVM, Node, Dart, and Jolt.\n   735\t- **No JVM-only reflection:** `yang.core.semantics` and `yang.core.prelude` use pure portable Clojure data transforms with zero `eval`, runtime `tools.reader`, or JVM reflection.\n   736\t\n   737\t### 8.2 Dependency graph and malleability (`docs/agents/malleability.md`)\n   738\t\n   739\tPreserves a strictly layered, cycle-free dependency graph verified with `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj`:\n   740\t\n   741\t```text\n   742\tLayer A (AST & Data Schemas):    yang.core.uast\n   743\tLayer B (Pure Composition):      yang.core.prelude, yang.core.semantics\n   744\tLayer C (Registry Admission):    yang.core.prelude-admission, yang.core.module, yang.core.publication\n   745\tLayer D (Shared Guest Modules):  yang.core.call, yang.rt.escape, yang.rt.float, yang.rt.int\n   746\tLayer E (Language Frontends):    yang.python.antlr.*, yang.typescript.antlr.*, yang.php.antlr.*,\n   747\t                                 yang.clojure.{prelude, bridge, core-module}\n   748\t```\n   749\t\n   750\t- **Frontend isolation:** Frontend-specific hook ABI contracts (like `yang.python.antlr.contract`) remain in Layer E, never in `yang.core.*`.\n   751\t- **Bounded public APIs:** Host namespaces maintain 2–5 `defn` entry points (`yang.core.semantics`: `validate-descriptor`, `capability-status`, `literal-node`, `hook-symbol`, `resolve-ambient`), and guest `yrt.*` modules bound their public export count cleanly (grouping only cohesive primitives per module rather than creating a sprawling grab-bag).\n   752\t\n   753\t### 8.3 Content-addressing and golden migration discipline\n   754\t\n   755\t1. **Address-neutral slices (P0, P2, P3):** `P0` preserves exact pre-change UAST bytes on frozen snapshots; `P2` emits byte-identical UAST for every default language profile; `P3` adds `clj.bridge`, `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`, and standalone `clojure.core` without changing `yang.clojure`'s default `library-for` / `clj` output or any existing language goldens.\n   756\t2. **One batched profile bump (`P1`):** Each `yrt.*` module (`yrt.escape`, `yrt.float`, `yrt.int`) is implemented and validated independently first, then activated across `py`, `js`, `php`, and `clj` in one coordinated profile bump so `:segment/blake3-*` goldens (`scanner_goldens.cljc`, `float_address_test.cljc`, `dht-import-v1.edn`, `clojure_callsite_test.cljc`, linked harnesses) refresh once.\n   757\t\n   758\t---\n   759\t\n   760\t## 9. Phased implementation roadmap and acceptance gates\n   761\t\n   762\t| Slice | Scope & deliverables | Golden impact | Concrete acceptance gate |\n   763\t|---|---|---|---|\n   764\t| **P0 — Composition plumbing & `defquoted` consolidation** | Consolidate `defquoted` into `yang.core.prelude`; implement `:yang.prelude/recipe` / `:yang.prelude/profile` composition, `validate-profile`, and `admit-profile` (with explicit `host-limits`, direct-root vs. transitive closure separation, operand sequencing, `init!` placement, tail marking, `:linear`/`:balanced` mode, and Clojure's custom preamble). | **Zero** (byte-identical emission) | Compare generated UAST/specs against frozen pre-change snapshots of `py`/`js`/`php`/`clj`/`yang.call`; test direct-vs.-transitive `:requires` closure validation (including transitive-only dependencies), missing transitive artifact/export refusal, `host-limits` numeric-floor enforcement, provenance-door/effect-ceiling exclusions, and projected-name collision refusal. |\n   765\t| **P1 — Layer 2a Tier 1 (`yrt.escape`, `yrt.float`, `yrt.int`)** | Implement the three stateless guest modules (frame indexing via `data/nth`, status-returning `yrt.float` boxed boundaries `neg-pow-result` / `floor-int-result` plus total `float-floor-raw` with zero raw-double callbacks and no `data/float64?` dependency); migrate `js`/`clj` from 4-slot to 5-slot contexts (`:handlers :depth :base :frame`); preserve open non-`:finally` (`:generator`) boundary dispatch; add `dsg__add`/`dsg__lte` guest helpers for bundled `clj`; activate across `py`, `js`, `php`, `clj` in one coordinated bump. | **One batched bump** | Unit tests for `yrt.*` on semantic/stack/register VMs; bundled/linked `yang.clojure` parity with source-defined `(defn get ...)` and active nested `try`/`throw`/`finally` frames; existing Python & PHP generator tests green; 4→5-slot migration tests; PHP `abandon-to` / `call-terminal` & normal `finally` replacement (`:py/None`, `:js/undefined`, `:php/null`, `nil`); `1.1 ** 6` bit-pattern parity (`fpow-half-raw` vs `fpow-base-raw`); exceptional `yrt.float` underflow (`0.5 ** -2000` -> `:yrt.float/underflow` + outer overflow policy), subnormal (`2.0 ** -1074` -> `5e-324`), normal zero (`2.0 ** -2000` -> `+0.0`), and out-of-range (`floor(1e30)`, `floor(NaN)`, `floor(Inf)`) witnesses under `%capture`/safepoints across 4 hosts; `yin.vm.integer` v4 three-reason translation without masking operational throws; independent concurrent `py`/`js`/`php`/`clj` tasks sharing `yrt.*`; bundled == linked + 4-host + CPython/Node/PHP oracle parity; `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj` clean. |\n   766\t| **P2 — Lowering parameterization (`yang.core.semantics` + frontend contracts)** | Implement generic `yang.core.semantics`; define `yang.python.antlr.contract` (then TS/PHP); refactor `yang.python.antlr.lower` to read literals/hooks (including comprehension accumulators with optional `:comp/finish`), capabilities, and projections from `:yang.semantics/descriptor` defaulting to `:yang.python/py-v1`. | **Zero** (byte-identical default output) | Byte-for-byte UAST equality test across the full corpus under `:yang.python/py-v1` (with `:comp/finish nil`); tests covering every supported lowering path and capability mode (`:cell`, `:single-assignment`, `:ambient-only`); validation of `:literals.*.overflow-op` and all hooks/projections against the descriptor's own selected `:ambient-modules` closure (refusing exports outside the selected closure); unqualified-hook rejection; reserved-door projection ban (including `raw-*`); refusal of typed `except E:` when `:control/except-typed :refused` and of generator expressions when `:control/generators :refused`. |\n   767\t| **P3 — `clojure.core` prelude for `yang.python` (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`)** | Add pure `data/float64?` (`yin.vm.data`) and `kind/namespace` (`yang.clojure/kind-module`); publish trusted Layer-2b `clj.bridge` (bundled `uast` & linked `module-uast`, zero change to `clj`); publish standalone portable `clojure.core` module (`§7.5`: cell-free linker exports, idempotent `init!` / `export`, 0-arg accessors, `raw-seq`/`raw-first`/`raw-rest`, canonical collection traversal, uniform `admit-key!`, portable `str`/`fresh-symbol`/`inc`/`dec`/`rem`/`not=`/`fn?`) + `clj.py` adapter + `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` descriptor; leave `yang.clojure`'s default `library-for` untouched; wire `yang.frontend` multi-revision catalog selection. | **Zero** on existing languages | 4-host numeric & `data/float64?` suite: `2.1 // 0.7 == 3.0`, `-0.0 // 2.0 == -0.0` (`data/content=`), `1.0 / 0.0` (`:zero-division`), `-(0.0)` (`-0.0`), `-(-0.0)` (`+0.0`), `2.0 + 1.0`, `2.0 * 3`, `5.0 - 2`, `inc(1.0)`, `2 ** -3`, negative/nonfinite `%`, fractional/infinite `**` refusal; minimum 53-bit floor (`:max-bits 53`) tests (`2.0 ** (2.0 ** 53)`, `rem` `:bit-limit` before `data/nth`, `integer/neg` bit-limit) producing guest errors never host `:wrong-type`; uniform `admit-key!` across literals + projected `assoc`/`assoc_in`/`get`/`get_in`/`conj`/`contains?`/`disj`/`merge`/`into`/`union`/`difference` + comprehensions (accepting `{\"a\": -0.0} == {\"a\": 0.0}`, `[0.0] == [-0.0]`, `[NaN] == [NaN]` and refusing `1.0`/`-0.0`/`NaN`/`[[-0.0]]` as keys/set elements on all 4 hosts); nonempty list, set, and dict comprehensions + bare `except:`; `fn?` aligned 1-to-1 with dynamic caller (false for raw host primitives/continuations/forged maps; true for authenticated cells) and `map?` false on callables; 4-step entry validation (non-callable `raise-exit` operational error, mismatched `:yang.call/callee` `:invalid-invocation`, unsupported `:binding-profile`, ordinary arity/named errors under `:yang.call/thrown`, normal `20` preserved); `lift-slice` publication of cell-free `clojure.core`, two importers in one task observing identical (`=`) cell reference and two tasks observing isolated cells; bundled == linked parity for `clj.bridge` retained protocol conditions and nested `clj → clj.py → clj` unwinds over `(clj/rt-ctx)`; deterministic 4-host `fresh-symbol`, `gensym`, `str` (`1.0`/`-0.0`/`NaN`/maps/keywords), canonical `keys`/`vals`/`seq`/`first`/`vec`, exact-int `nth`, and excluded `var?`/`resolve`; lexical shadowing of projected names and per-module `globals` isolation. |\n   768\t| **P4 — Tier-2 shared modules (`yrt.gen`, `yrt.safepoint`)** | Extract parameterized `yrt.gen` (preserving Python `:base` rebasing vs. PHP direct context restoration and refcount cleanup) and `yrt.safepoint` (`stream/poll!` skeleton for `pysp`/`jssp`). | **One bump** (deferred) | Generator + safepoint parity suites across VMs/hosts, preserving PHP lifecycle/cleanup policy and non-rebasing context behavior vs. Python rebasing. |\n   769\t\n   770\t---\n   771\t\n   772\t## 10. Open owner decisions\n   773\t\n   774\t1. **D1 — Local mutation model for `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`:**\n   775\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* `:mutation/locals :cell` (task-heap cells holding pure persistent Clojure values, matching Python parameter binding, unbound reads, reassignment, loops, and `nonlocal` with per-module `globals` cells). Keep `:single-assignment` as a separate restricted profile.\n   776\t   - *Option B:* `:mutation/locals :single-assignment` only (refuses local reassignment).\n   777\t2. **D2 — Namespace prefix for Layer-2a shared modules:**\n   778\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* `yrt.*` (`yrt.escape`, `yrt.float`, `yrt.int`, `yrt.gen`, `yrt.safepoint`) matching `yang.typescript.md` §17 and `yang.php.md` §9, implemented in Clojure under `src/cljc/yang/rt/*.cljc`.\n   779\t   - *Option B:* `yang.rt.*` for both Clojure namespaces and linker module names.\n   780\t3. **D3 — Python float tagging during P1:**\n   781\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* Retain `{:py/float x}` behind a 2-line `py` boundary adapter around `yrt.float` so P1 stays a pure runtime extraction without shifting Python value semantics or equality.\n   782\t   - *Option B:* Migrate Python to untagged `data/float64` carriers in P1.\n   783\t4. **D4 — Batching P1 (`yrt.escape` + `yrt.float` + `yrt.int`) vs. per-module bumps:**\n   784\t   - *Option A (Recommended conditionally — Architect concurred):* Implement and test each `yrt.*` extraction independently first, then activate all three in one coordinated profile bump so `:segment/blake3-*` goldens refresh once.\n   785\t   - *Option B:* Ship each `yrt.*` module as a separate profile bump.\n   786\t5. **D5 — Cross-syntax identifier mapping for Clojure names (`?`, `!`, `-`):**\n   787\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* Curated `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` table validated against exact exports, lexical precedence, primitive callable projections, and reserved-door bans.\n   788\t   - *Option B:* Algorithmic mangling rule (`_q` / `_bang`).\n   789\t6. **D6 — Publishing `clojure.core` as a standalone linked module:**\n   790\t   - *Option A (Constrained, Recommended — Architect concurred):* Publish the portable `clojure.core` subset (`§7.5`) with per-task instantiation in P3 for `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` and future profiles, while keeping `yang.clojure`'s default `library-for` bundling unchanged in P3 (migrating `yang.clojure` separately later so P3 moves zero Clojure goldens).\n   791\t   - *Option B:* Copy needed `library` definitions into `clj.py`.\n   792\t7. **D7 — Float exponentiation rounding (`py`/`js` half-power vs. `php` base squaring):**\n   793\t   - *Option A (Recommended for P1 — Architect concurred):* Export both `yrt.float/fpow-half-raw` (selected by `:half` in `neg-pow-result`) and `yrt.float/fpow-base-raw` (selected by `:base`) so P1 preserves bit-exact parity (`1.1 ** 6`: `0x1.c585058dde7acp+0` for `py`/`js` vs `0x1.c585058dde7abp+0` for `php`) across all existing oracles.\n   794\t   - *Option B:* Explicitly approve unifying PHP onto `fpow-half-raw` (or `py`/`js` onto `fpow-base-raw`) and update the affected language's oracle departure ledger.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
