{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'ex-info|clj.py/export|clj.py/init\"'!|runtime-profile|arity|signature'\"' docs/design/yang.preludes.md | head -95\"","aggregated_output":"47:2. **Hardcoded syntax-to-prelude coupling:** A frontend lowering currently assumes one fixed runtime profile. Even though `yang.frontend` (`src/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc`) already tracks `:yang.frontend/grammar`, `:yang.frontend/lowering-profile`, `:yang.frontend/runtime-profile`, and `:yang.frontend/support-profile` independently in its manifest, a lowering cannot today treat its target prelude as a configurable library—such as lowering Python syntax onto `clojure.core` and persistent Yin values.\n60:2. **Interpretation Creates Semantics:** A CST packet carries syntax only; its runtime meaning emerges from the tuple `(cst-packet, lowering-profile, semantics-descriptor, runtime-profile)`. Interpreting one Python CST under `:yang.python/py-v1` (CPython semantics) versus `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` (Clojure persistent-data semantics) is a direct realization of \"one truth, many perspectives.\"\n61:3. **Code and State are Datoms (and Unitarity / Derive-Don't-Persist):**\n62:   - Lowering preserves source CST identity; compiled UAST roots under different preludes have distinct content addresses (or identical addresses when two descriptors emit identical UAST) linked by explicit provenance datoms pinning `(cst-address, lowering-profile, semantics-descriptor, runtime-profile, unit-address)`.\n196:   - To avoid silently breaking PHP or Python/JS oracle parity in P1, `yrt.float` exports **both** `fpow-half-raw` (selected by `:half`, for `py`/`js`/`clj.py`) and `fpow-base-raw` (selected by `:base`, for `php`) — see owner decision D7 if a future unified rounding rule is ever approved.\n219:- Every other refusal (`:arity`, `:wrong-type`, `:out-of-range`, `:syntax`, `:zero-division`, `:negative-count`, `:negative-exponent`) **throws** a host operational failure indicating a caller-side defect (`integer.cljc:93–100`) and **MUST NOT** be caught or relabeled into guest exceptions.\n309:6. **Dual-emitter preservation & Parity Law:**\n312:   - **Bundled vs. Linked Parity Law:** Any program compiled under a composed prelude MUST produce identical outcomes in bundled and linked modes across the semantic, stack, and register VMs (and the AST walker once L-b lands).\n335:  1. Its **fixed Hook ABI table** (`{hook-key {:arity n :required-by [...]}}`) specifying exact parameter conventions and structural lowering shapes for that frontend's grammar.\n470:  \"ex_info\"   {:module 'clj.py,       :export 'ex-info,   :kind :cell-accessor}}}\n487:     - Verifies every such symbol is namespace-qualified (for hooks and literal strategies), matches the frontend-authorized role and arity in `frontend-contract`, and exists as an **exact published export in the selected, address-verified closure** (or in a host module of `registry` explicitly required by that selected closure and permitted by `frontend-contract`, or an allowed non-reserved VM primitive). An export belonging to an unrelated manifest somewhere else in `artifact-store` outside the descriptor's selected closure is **rejected**!\n511:- `:yang.frontend/runtime-profile` pins the content address of the resolved `:yang.prelude/profile` manifest.\n512:- Compilation provenance records `(cst-address, lowering-profile, runtime-profile, unit-address)` as data; note that distinct descriptors may legitimately yield identical UAST addresses on simple programs (many-to-one), so provenance retains the exact compilation tuple rather than inferring the descriptor from the UAST address alone.\n537:*Truth-in-advertising invariant:* `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` explicitly declares Clojure truthiness, persistent immutable collections, non-numeric booleans, and kind-strict equality as its support profile — never CPython parity.\n594:     - **Refused keys / set elements at ANY nesting depth:** any `data/float64?` value (`0.0`, `-0.0`, `1.0`, `NaN`, `±Inf`, or nested `[[-0.0]]`, `{\"a\" 1.0}`), lists/seqs (`seq?`, preventing Jing/host list-vs-vector collisions when used as map keys or set elements), host closures/continuations, and `:cell-ref` handles — raising guest error `{:clj.py/error :unsupported-key :key k}` (`ex-info` in `clojure.core`).\n608:Rather than pretending `clj/*` shares identical signatures with `py/*`, the frontend keeps its fixed **Python Lowering Hook ABI** (`yang.python.antlr.contract`) and `clj.py` implements every hook with compatible arity and semantics:\n610:| Hook key | Frontend ABI signature | `clj.py` implementation |\n617:| `:ctrl/try` | `[body handler orelse]` | **3-arg signature** calling `yrt.escape/try-orelse` on `(clj/rt-ctx)` (sharing Clojure's exception domain by design), preserving Python `try` / `except` / `else`. |\n625:| `:unit/run-main` | `[body-fn]` | Calls idempotent `(clj/init!)`, `(clojure.core/init!)`, and `(clj.py/init!)`; allocates a **fresh per-unit `globals` cell** (`(cell/new {})`) and `globals-fn`; invokes `(body-fn globals globals-fn)` inside a top-level handler on `(clj/rt-ctx)`; returns the value **verbatim without stripping `[:yin.k/ok ...]`** so ordinary Python data shaped like `[:yin.k/ok 42]` passes through uncorrupted. |\n635:- `clj.bridge` owns the private provenance doors (`cell/dsg__new-provenance`, `cell/dsg__provenance`) inside **both** its linked (`module-uast`) and bundled (`uast`) emitters (preserving §5.2 Bundled vs. Linked Parity Law!), never exporting them and keeping them strictly out of `yrt.*`, `clj.py`, and Layer-2c `clojure.core`.\n662:     - Installs the exception handler on `(clj/rt-ctx)` **before** argument binding so ordinary named-arg / positional-arity errors share the same boundary (`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1244–1256` and `yang.antlr.md:3861–3867` §8.10.7): inside `try-value`, checks `:yang.call/named` and positional/varargs arity against `:spec` (raising local guest binding exceptions via `clj/raise` so they cross under **`:yang.call/thrown`**) and evaluates `(bind-and-run positional named)`.\n765:| **P1 — Layer 2a Tier 1 (`yrt.escape`, `yrt.float`, `yrt.int`)** | Implement the three stateless guest modules (frame indexing via `data/nth`, status-returning `yrt.float` boxed boundaries `neg-pow-result` / `floor-int-result` plus total `float-floor-raw` with zero raw-double callbacks and no `data/float64?` dependency); migrate `js`/`clj` from 4-slot to 5-slot contexts (`:handlers :depth :base :frame`); preserve open non-`:finally` (`:generator`) boundary dispatch; add `dsg__add`/`dsg__lte` guest helpers for bundled `clj`; activate across `py`, `js`, `php`, `clj` in one coordinated bump. | **One batched bump** | Unit tests for `yrt.*` on semantic/stack/register VMs; bundled/linked `yang.clojure` parity with source-defined `(defn get ...)` and active nested `try`/`throw`/`finally` frames; existing Python & PHP generator tests green; 4→5-slot migration tests; PHP `abandon-to` / `call-terminal` & normal `finally` replacement (`:py/None`, `:js/undefined`, `:php/null`, `nil`); `1.1 ** 6` bit-pattern parity (`fpow-half-raw` vs `fpow-base-raw`); exceptional `yrt.float` underflow (`0.5 ** -2000` -> `:yrt.float/underflow` + outer overflow policy), subnormal (`2.0 ** -1074` -> `5e-324`), normal zero (`2.0 ** -2000` -> `+0.0`), and out-of-range (`floor(1e30)`, `floor(NaN)`, `floor(Inf)`) witnesses under `%capture`/safepoints across 4 hosts; `yin.vm.integer` v4 three-reason translation without masking operational throws; independent concurrent `py`/`js`/`php`/`clj` tasks sharing `yrt.*`; bundled == linked + 4-host + CPython/Node/PHP oracle parity; `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj` clean. |\n767:| **P3 — `clojure.core` prelude for `yang.python` (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`)** | Add pure `data/float64?` (`yin.vm.data`) and `kind/namespace` (`yang.clojure/kind-module`); publish trusted Layer-2b `clj.bridge` (bundled `uast` & linked `module-uast`, zero change to `clj`); publish standalone portable `clojure.core` module (`§7.5`: cell-free linker exports, idempotent `init!` / `export`, 0-arg accessors, `raw-seq`/`raw-first`/`raw-rest`, canonical collection traversal, uniform `admit-key!`, portable `str`/`fresh-symbol`/`inc`/`dec`/`rem`/`not=`/`fn?`) + `clj.py` adapter + `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` descriptor; leave `yang.clojure`'s default `library-for` untouched; wire `yang.frontend` multi-revision catalog selection. | **Zero** on existing languages | 4-host numeric & `data/float64?` suite: `2.1 // 0.7 == 3.0`, `-0.0 // 2.0 == -0.0` (`data/content=`), `1.0 / 0.0` (`:zero-division`), `-(0.0)` (`-0.0`), `-(-0.0)` (`+0.0`), `2.0 + 1.0`, `2.0 * 3`, `5.0 - 2`, `inc(1.0)`, `2 ** -3`, negative/nonfinite `%`, fractional/infinite `**` refusal; minimum 53-bit floor (`:max-bits 53`) tests (`2.0 ** (2.0 ** 53)`, `rem` `:bit-limit` before `data/nth`, `integer/neg` bit-limit) producing guest errors never host `:wrong-type`; uniform `admit-key!` across literals + projected `assoc`/`assoc_in`/`get`/`get_in`/`conj`/`contains?`/`disj`/`merge`/`into`/`union`/`difference` + comprehensions (accepting `{\"a\": -0.0} == {\"a\": 0.0}`, `[0.0] == [-0.0]`, `[NaN] == [NaN]` and refusing `1.0`/`-0.0`/`NaN`/`[[-0.0]]` as keys/set elements on all 4 hosts); nonempty list, set, and dict comprehensions + bare `except:`; `fn?` aligned 1-to-1 with dynamic caller (false for raw host primitives/continuations/forged maps; true for authenticated cells) and `map?` false on callables; 4-step entry validation (non-callable `raise-exit` operational error, mismatched `:yang.call/callee` `:invalid-invocation`, unsupported `:binding-profile`, ordinary arity/named errors under `:yang.call/thrown`, normal `20` preserved); `lift-slice` publication of cell-free `clojure.core`, two importers in one task observing identical (`=`) cell reference and two tasks observing isolated cells; bundled == linked parity for `clj.bridge` retained protocol conditions and nested `clj → clj.py → clj` unwinds over `(clj/rt-ctx)`; deterministic 4-host `fresh-symbol`, `gensym`, `str` (`1.0`/`-0.0`/`NaN`/maps/keywords), canonical `keys`/`vals`/`seq`/`first`/`vec`, exact-int `nth`, and excluded `var?`/`resolve`; lexical shadowing of projected names and per-module `globals` isolation. |\n768:| **P4 — Tier-2 shared modules (`yrt.gen`, `yrt.safepoint`)** | Extract parameterized `yrt.gen` (preserving Python `:base` rebasing vs. PHP direct context restoration and refcount cleanup) and `yrt.safepoint` (`stream/poll!` skeleton for `pysp`/`jssp`). | **One bump** (deferred) | Generator + safepoint parity suites across VMs/hosts, preserving PHP lifecycle/cleanup policy and non-rebasing context behavior vs. Python rebasing. |\n793:   - *Option A (Recommended for P1 — Architect concurred):* Export both `yrt.float/fpow-half-raw` (selected by `:half` in `neg-pow-result`) and `yrt.float/fpow-base-raw` (selected by `:base`) so P1 preserves bit-exact parity (`1.1 ** 6`: `0x1.c585058dde7acp+0` for `py`/`js` vs `0x1.c585058dde7abp+0` for `php`) across all existing oracles.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
