.core, :export 'filter,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n460:  \"reduce\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'reduce,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n461:  \"into\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'into,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n462:  \"keys\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'keys,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n463:  \"vals\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'vals,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n464:  \"merge\"     {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'merge,     :kind :cell-accessor}\n465:  \"is_empty\"  {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'empty?,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n466:  \"is_nil\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'nil?,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n467:  \"is_map\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'map?,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n468:  \"is_vector\" {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'vector?,   :kind :cell-accessor}\n469:  \"is_set\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'set?,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n470:  \"ex_info\"   {:module 'clj.py,       :export 'ex-info,   :kind :cell-accessor}}}\n481:     3. **`:yang.semantics/ambient-projections`** (resolved via `clj.py/global-get` fallback to the module's explicit projected lookup map, calling `(m/e)` for `:kind :cell-accessor` entries, or refused at runtime/admission if absent).\n487:     - Verifies every such symbol is namespace-qualified (for hooks and literal strategies), matches the frontend-authorized role and arity in `frontend-contract`, and exists as an **exact published export in the selected, address-verified closure** (or in a host module of `registry` explicitly required by that selected closure and permitted by `frontend-contract`, or an allowed non-reserved VM primitive). An export belonging to an unrelated manifest somewhere else in `artifact-store` outside the descriptor's selected closure is **rejected**!\n488:     - For `:ambient-projections`, checks unique source names and, when `:kind :cell-accessor` (the default), verifies that module `m` exports both the named 0-arg accessor `e` and its idempotent task table initializers (`init!`, `export`).\n590:4. **Uniform portable key/element domain (`admit-key!`) & recursive equality (`clj.py/eq`, `clj.py/ne`):**\n592:   - **One uniform `v1` portable key/element admission gate (`admit-key!`):** Enforced across BOTH `clj.py` (`map-from`, `set-from`, `get-item`, `comp-set-add`, `comp-dict-set`) AND standalone `clojure.core` (`assoc`, `assoc-in`, `update`, `update-in`, `get`, `get-in`, `contains?`, `conj` on maps/sets, `disj`, `merge`, `into` when targeting maps/sets, `union`, `difference`, `hash-map`, `set`):\n613:| `:env/global-get` | `[globals-cell name]` | Reads the unit's **per-module** `globals-cell` first; on miss, falls back to `clj.py`'s explicit `:ambient-projections` lookup table (invoking the 0-arg accessor `(m/e)` for `:kind :cell-accessor` entries to obtain the stable task-local authenticated callable cell); on miss there, raises guest `NameError`-equivalent map `{:clj.py/error :name-error :name name}`. Keeps distinct compiled modules isolated instead of sharing one flat `clj.rt/globals` map. |\n623:| `:comp/list-append`, `:comp/set-add`, `:comp/dict-set` | `[acc val]`, `[acc val]`, `[acc k v]` | Reads `(cell/get acc)`, validates set elements / dict keys via `admit-key!`, updates via `(cell/set! acc (conj cur val))` / `(assoc cur k v)`, and returns `:py/None` (in `clj.py`, `nil`). |\n685:     - `str`: explicit 4-host deterministic renderer (never delegating arbitrary values to host `kind/str`!): `nil -> \"\"`; strings verbatim; booleans `\"true\"`/`\"false\"`; exact integers via `integer/format` + `yrt.int/check-limit`; `data/float64?` via pure leaf unwrap + `integer/float-digits` + `yrt.float` decimal layout (`zeros`/`exp-text`) with explicit `\"NaN\"`, `\"Infinity\"`, `\"-Infinity\"`, `\"0.0\"`, `\"-0.0\"` branches so `1.0` renders `\"1.0\"` (never JS `\"1\"`) across all 4 hosts; keywords (`\":\"`) & symbols via `kind/namespace` + `kind/name`; vectors/lists recursively; maps and sets in canonical key order (`canonical-compare`); authenticated callable cells as `\"#<fn>\"`.\n686:     - **Canonical map/set traversal (`canonical-compare`) — eliminating host iteration order:** Standalone `clojure.core` defines a deterministic total order over the admitted `v1` key/element domain (`§7.2`: type rank `nil < boolean < exact integer (integer/compare) < string (data/str-compare) < keyword (kind/namespace, kind/name via data/str-compare) < symbol < vector < map < set`). `raw-seq`, `seq`, `first`, `rest`, `vec`, `keys`, `vals`, `str`, `reduce`, `map`, `filter`, `remove`, `into`, `merge`, `union`, and `difference` all normalize map entry pairs `[k v]` and set elements into canonical sorted order before producing ordered sequences — guaranteeing identical `keys`, `vals`, `vec`, and `seq` results on JVM, CLJS/Node, CLJD/Dart, and Jolt.\n688:     - **Uniform portable key/element gate (`admit-key!`):** `assoc`, `assoc-in`, `update`, `update-in`, `get`, `get-in`, `contains?`, `conj` (on maps and sets), `disj`, `merge`, `into` (targeting maps/sets), `union`, `difference`, `hash-map`, and `set` all enforce `admit-key!` (`§7.2`: recursively refusing any `data/float64?` or `seq?` key/element on all 4 hosts).\n692:   - **Primitive callable projections:** thin cell-backed callable wrappers over VM primitives (`nil?`, `empty?`, `not`, `first`, `conj`, `assoc`, `get`, `vec`, enforcing `admit-key!` on `conj`/`assoc`/`get` for maps/sets) so Python source can either call `is_empty(xs)` directly OR pass `is_empty` as a higher-order callback to `filter`/`map`.\n693:3. **Linker-safe export table, idempotent `init!`, 0-arg cell accessors, and reconciled call path:**\n698:     4. **Public 0-arg cell-accessor exports:** For every public library function `<name>` (including projected `empty?`, `nil?`, `map`, `filter`, `reduce`, etc.), `clojure.core` exports a pure cell-free lambda `(fn [] (clojure.core/export (quote <name>)))`. Because these exports are pure functions, `lift-slice` succeeds cleanly; `validate-descriptor` verifies every projected name directly against the published manifest; and callers (`clj.py`, `py`, `js`, `php`, bundled or linked) invoke `(clojure.core/<name>)` to retrieve the stable task-local cell and call it via `clj.bridge/invoke-callable` / `yang.call/invoke`.\n699:     5. **Separately named internal adapter entries (`raw-*`):** Pure implementation entries (`clojure.core/raw-seq`, `clojure.core/raw-first`, `clojure.core/raw-rest`) are exported strictly under the reserved `raw-*` internal adapter prefix (banned from `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` by `validate-descriptor`), allowing trusted Layer-2b hooks such as `clj.py/for-each` to iterate directly without going through a 0-arg cell accessor.\n767:| **P3 — `clojure.core` prelude for `yang.python` (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`)** | Add pure `data/float64?` (`yin.vm.data`) and `kind/namespace` (`yang.clojure/kind-module`); publish trusted Layer-2b `clj.bridge` (bundled `uast` & linked `module-uast`, zero change to `clj`); publish standalone portable `clojure.core` module (`§7.5`: cell-free linker exports, idempotent `init!` / `export`, 0-arg accessors, `raw-seq`/`raw-first`/`raw-rest`, canonical collection traversal, uniform `admit-key!`, portable `str`/`fresh-symbol`/`inc`/`dec`/`rem`/`not=`/`fn?`) + `clj.py` adapter + `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` descriptor; leave `yang.clojure`'s default `library-for` untouched; wire `yang.frontend` multi-revision catalog selection. | **Zero** on existing languages | 4-host numeric & `data/float64?` suite: `2.1 // 0.7 == 3.0`, `-0.0 // 2.0 == -0.0` (`data/content=`), `1.0 / 0.0` (`:zero-division`), `-(0.0)` (`-0.0`), `-(-0.0)` (`+0.0`), `2.0 + 1.0`, `2.0 * 3`, `5.0 - 2`, `inc(1.0)`, `2 ** -3`, negative/nonfinite `%`, fractional/infinite `**` refusal; minimum 53-bit floor (`:max-bits 53`) tests (`2.0 ** (2.0 ** 53)`, `rem` `:bit-limit` before `data/nth`, `integer/neg` bit-limit) producing guest errors never host `:wrong-type`; uniform `admit-key!` across literals + projected `assoc`/`assoc_in`/`get`/`get_in`/`conj`/`contains?`/`disj`/`merge`/`into`/`union`/`difference` + comprehensions (accepting `{\"a\": -0.0} == {\"a\": 0.0}`, `[0.0] == [-0.0]`, `[NaN] == [NaN]` and refusing `1.0`/`-0.0`/`NaN`/`[[-0.0]]` as keys/set elements on all 4 hosts); nonempty list, set, and dict comprehensions + bare `except:`; `fn?` aligned 1-to-1 with dynamic caller (false for raw host primitives/continuations/forged maps; true for authenticated cells) and `map?` false on callables; 4-step entry validation (non-callable `raise-exit` operational error, mismatched `:yang.call/callee` `:invalid-invocation`, unsupported `:binding-profile`, ordinary arity/named errors under `:yang.call/thrown`, normal `20` preserved); `lift-slice` publication of cell-free `clojure.core`, two importers in one task observing identical (`=`) cell reference and two tasks observing isolated cells; bundled == linked parity for `clj.bridge` retained protocol conditions and nested `clj → clj.py → clj` unwinds over `(clj/rt-ctx)`; deterministic 4-host `fresh-symbol`, `gensym`, `str` (`1.0`/`-0.0`/`NaN`/maps/keywords), canonical `keys`/`vals`/`seq`/`first`/`vec`, exact-int `nth`, and excluded `var?`/`resolve`; lexical shadowing of projected names and per-module `globals` isolation. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
