{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc | sed -n '38,78p;407,460p'\"","aggregated_output":"    38\t\n    39\t\n    40\t(defn- walk-path\n    41\t  \"Descend a registry's :modules map along path, a sequence of symbols.\n    42\t\n    43\t   Namespace segments step through plain maps until the path reaches a\n    44\t   module entry (a map carrying :manifest); the remaining segments read\n    45\t   that entry's task-local lowered `:bindings` when it holds them -- a\n    46\t   linked module (yin.vm.linker.md section 8.3) -- and its `:slice`\n    47\t   otherwise, which for a host module is the host values themselves, so\n    48\t   a binding name resolves to its export.\"\n    49\t  [node path]\n    50\t  (if (seq path)\n    51\t    (if (and (map? node) (contains? node :manifest))\n    52\t      (if-let [child (get node (first path))]\n    53\t        (walk-path child (rest path))\n    54\t        (get-in node (into [(if (contains? node :bindings) :bindings :slice)]\n    55\t                           path)))\n    56\t      (when-let [child (get node (first path))]\n    57\t        (walk-path child (rest path))))\n    58\t    node))\n    59\t\n    60\t\n    61\t(defn module-entry\n    62\t  \"The registry entry of module `module-name` in `modules` (a registry's\n    63\t   `:modules` map), or nil when the dotted path reaches no module entry.\"\n    64\t  [modules module-name]\n    65\t  (let [node (reduce (fn [node seg] (when (map? node) (get node seg)))\n    66\t                     modules\n    67\t                     (symbol->path module-name))]\n    68\t    (when (and (map? node) (contains? node :manifest)) node)))\n    69\t\n    70\t\n    71\t(defn assoc-module\n    72\t  \"Return registry with `entry` installed as module `module-name`.\"\n    73\t  [registry module-name entry]\n    74\t  (let [registry (or registry (empty-registry))\n    75\t        path (into [:modules] (symbol->path module-name))\n    76\t        children (into {} (filter (comp symbol? key)) (get-in registry path))]\n    77\t    (assoc-in registry path (merge children entry))))\n    78\t\n   407\t(defn authentic-cell?\n   408\t  \"The pure query the cell-ref ruling of record added: does the heap\n   409\t   issue `c` as a cell reference? The engine answers the same\n   410\t   heap+seal predicate `check-ref!` consults, as a boolean, so compiled\n   411\t   call routing can ask the issuer instead of guessing from a value's\n   412\t   shape. Non-fatal, state unchanged.\"\n   413\t  [c]\n   414\t  (make-effect :cell/authentic? {:cell c}))\n   415\t\n   416\t\n   417\t(defn new-provenance-cell\n   418\t  \"The privileged mint: allocate a fresh sealed cell holding `value` with\n   419\t   `provenance` installed in its private `:provenance` sibling, atomically.\n   420\t   `provenance` must be non-nil and is otherwise opaque to the VM. Only the\n   421\t   mint attaches provenance, and only at allocation. Not a guest surface:\n   422\t   the name is compiler-private (`dsg__`).\"\n   423\t  [value provenance]\n   424\t  (make-effect :cell/new-provenance {:val value, :provenance provenance}))\n   425\t\n   426\t\n   427\t(defn provenance-cell\n   428\t  \"The private reader: the `:provenance` a live, authenticated, marked cell\n   429\t   carries, or nil for anything else — an unmarked cell, a forged or dead\n   430\t   reference, or a non-reference. Never fatal, never mutating, and the\n   431\t   engine learns no frontend semantics from the slot. Not a guest surface:\n   432\t   the name is compiler-private (`dsg__`).\"\n   433\t  [candidate]\n   434\t  (make-effect :cell/provenance {:cell candidate}))\n   435\t\n   436\t\n   437\t(def cell-module\n   438\t  \"The `cell` module definition. Registering it is a composition step. The\n   439\t   two `dsg__` bindings are the compiler-private provenance mint and reader:\n   440\t   guest code may neither spell nor construct their names.\"\n   441\t  {'new new-cell, 'get get-cell, 'set! set-cell!, 'authentic? authentic-cell?,\n   442\t   'dsg__new-provenance new-provenance-cell,\n   443\t   'dsg__provenance provenance-cell})\n   444\t\n   445\t\n   446\t(def cell-profiles\n   447\t  \"UCF 7.5.2 profiles for the `cell` module's bindings: each an\n   448\t   `:effectful` pure effect constructor declaring its one effect kind.\"\n   449\t  {'new (vm/primitive-profile 'new :effectful [1] #{:cell/new} :none)\n   450\t   'get (vm/primitive-profile 'get :effectful [1] #{:cell/get} :none)\n   451\t   'set! (vm/primitive-profile 'set! :effectful [2] #{:cell/set!} :none)\n   452\t   'authentic? (vm/primitive-profile 'authentic? :effectful [1]\n   453\t                                     #{:cell/authentic?} :none)\n   454\t   'dsg__new-provenance (vm/primitive-profile 'dsg__new-provenance\n   455\t                                              :effectful [2]\n   456\t                                              #{:cell/new-provenance} :none)\n   457\t   'dsg__provenance (vm/primitive-profile 'dsg__provenance\n   458\t                                          :effectful [1]\n   459\t                                          #{:cell/provenance} :none)})\n   460\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
