{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc | sed -n '330,371p;1827,1872p'\"","aggregated_output":"   330\t\n   331\t;; Primitive operations\n   332\t;; Arithmetic and comparison ops are direct clojure.core references.\n   333\t;; Wrapped only where VM semantics require it:\n   334\t;; - rest: clojure.core/rest returns a lazy seq; wrapped to return a vector\n   335\t;;   so that conj appends rather than prepends.\n   336\t;; - /: only the JVM throws on an integral zero divisor; JS and Dart divide\n   337\t;;   IEEE-754 and yield Infinity, so checked-divide makes the error\n   338\t;;   host-uniform.\n   339\t;; - require: returns an effect descriptor consumed by the engine.\n   340\t;; There is no `yin/def` primitive: a definition is syntax (Rule R).\n   341\t(defn- checked-divide\n   342\t  \"clojure.core `/` except a zero divisor throws on every host.\n   343\t\n   344\t   JVM `/` throws `Divide by zero` for integral division only; JS and Dart\n   345\t   yield Infinity, so `(/ 1 0)` through the VM silently evaluated to `##Inf`\n   346\t   on those hosts. The REPL corpus pins divide-by-zero as an error with this\n   347\t   text on both evaluators (docs/design/yin.vm.divergence-register.md).\n   348\t   JS and Dart cannot distinguish `0` from `0.0`, so no rule reproduces the\n   349\t   JVM's double-division `##Inf` cross-host; the uniform error is the\n   350\t   contract.\"\n   351\t  ([x] (checked-divide 1 x))\n   352\t  ([x y]\n   353\t   (when (and (number? y) (zero? y))\n   354\t     (throw (ex-info \"Divide by zero\" {:divisor y})))\n   355\t   (/ x y))\n   356\t  ([x y & more] (reduce checked-divide (checked-divide x y) more)))\n   357\t\n   358\t\n   359\t(defn primitive-profile\n   360\t  \"Build UCF §7.5.2's published profile record for `name`.\n   361\t\n   362\t   The address covers the name and all four semantic declarations. The name\n   363\t   remains the registry key rather than being duplicated in the returned\n   364\t   record. Profile values contain no host function objects and are therefore\n   365\t   ordinary portable data.\"\n   366\t  [name class arities effects host-state]\n   367\t  (let [description {:yin.k/name name,\n   368\t                     :yin.k/class class,\n   369\t                     :yin.k/arities (vec arities),\n   370\t                     :yin.k/effects (set effects),\n   371\t                     :yin.k/host-state host-state}\n  1827\t   current semantic contract: the three value queries as extracted,\n  1828\t   and the effect-raising\n  1829\t   tags/mnemonics normalized through the footprint table's `dir` direction\n  1830\t   before any union, so the union is over one vocabulary (§7.7.1).\"\n  1831\t  [db queries dir]\n  1832\t  (let [table (get-in footprint-table [semantic-contract dir])]\n  1833\t    {:store-keys (extract (:store-keys queries) db),\n  1834\t     :ffi-ops (extract (:ffi-ops queries) db),\n  1835\t     :parked-ids (extract (:parked-ids queries) db),\n  1836\t     :effects (into #{} (mapcat table) (extract (:effect-raisers queries) db))}))\n  1837\t\n  1838\t\n  1839\t(defn ast-requirements\n  1840\t  \"§7.7's syntactic requirement set from a tree relation `$ast` — a\n  1841\t   `query/relation` over the flat rows of the reachable trees (e.g.\n  1842\t   `(vals (:rows (ast->semantic-bytecode ast)))`, unioned across trees):\n  1843\t   store keys, FFI ops, parked ids, and effect identifiers, effects\n  1844\t   already normalized by the footprint table. These are the fields of\n  1845\t   `:yin.k/requires` the syntactic queries fill; free names are\n  1846\t   `free-names`, and the value/name/module parts of UCF §7.6.1's fixed\n  1847\t   point remain the walk that consumes this.\"\n  1848\t  [db]\n  1849\t  (requirements db ast-extraction-queries :tags))\n  1850\t\n  1851\t\n  1852\t(def ^:private many-attrs #{:yin/operands :yin/args :yin/params})\n  1853\t\n  1854\t\n  1855\t(defn index-datoms\n  1856\t  \"Index AST datoms by entity.\n  1857\t   Returns {:by-entity map, :get-attr fn, :root-id int}, plus\n  1858\t   `:error {:rule :dangling-root :entity e}` when the root fact names an\n  1859\t   entity with no `:yin/type`.\n  1860\t\n  1861\t   The root is the entity of the last `:yin/root` fact in batch order. A\n  1862\t   batch with no root fact falls back to the structural heuristic below. A\n  1863\t   dangling root is recorded, not thrown: the index still names it, and\n  1864\t   decoding it is what fails loudly.\n  1865\t\n  1866\t   Optional opts:\n  1867\t   - :by-entity precomputed {eid [datom ...]} index\n  1868\t   - :root-id explicit root entity id override\"\n  1869\t  ([ast-as-datoms] (index-datoms ast-as-datoms {}))\n  1870\t  ([ast-as-datoms {:keys [by-entity root-id]}]\n  1871\t   (let [datoms (vec ast-as-datoms)\n  1872\t         by-entity (or by-entity (group-by first datoms))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
