{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'cell-backed|condition-shaped|closure|§7.5' collab/yang-base/1795196337796-architect-yang-preludes-design-r3.gpt-6.2-astra.findings.md | tail -17\"","aggregated_output":"15:**Five r2 findings are `CONFIRMED-FIXED`. F1, F3, and F4 remain `OPEN`.** The value-returning exception boundary, cell-backed closure construction, vector frame access, boxed float status interface, and active effect-ceiling example each resolve the specific defect reported in r2.\n27:| F3 | Source-level callable admission before structural invocation | **OPEN** | The specified sequence of checks is sound for the profile’s stated cell-backed interop surface, including rejection of unauthenticated maps. The supplied guest definition uses `and`, which the designated prelude emitter lowers as an ordinary application. Also, standalone `fn?` permits a raw-callable alternative that its dynamic caller rejects. [Admission predicate](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:591) · [Standalone predicate](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:628) |\n29:| F5 | Dynamic closure construction and internal higher-order calls | **CONFIRMED-FIXED** | The construction rule explicitly covers closures created during `comp` and `partial`. It preserves the returned cell’s identity. Static sibling calls use internal lambdas, while dynamic callback calls use the public invocation convention. The separate linker projection and provenance-ownership issues below concern how that contract is reached. [Construction and dispatch](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:633) |\n41:| **#9 — Recipe/profile separation and verified closure** | **The r2 correction remains in place.** The resolved profile pins the owning root and the design requires verified dependency manifests. Admission still needs an explicit source for the installed numeric limits, and descriptor targets must resolve against the selected closure. [Profile and closure](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:266) |\n51:| **HIGH** | [yang.preludes.md:594](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:594), [line 628](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:628) | The common emitter recognizes `if`, `let`, and a small set of other forms. It emits `and` as an application, and `and` has no standard VM primitive binding. The displayed predicate therefore cannot provide the required short circuit as written. Separately, `data/callable?` includes host functions and continuations. The optional `fn?` branch can report true for a value the standalone higher-order dispatcher refuses. [Emitter](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc:82) · [VM primitives](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:396) · [Applicability predicate](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc:456) | Emit nested `if` nodes or explicitly expand short-circuit syntax before emission. Use the same source admission predicate in `fn?`, ordinary calls, and higher-order calls. Keep raw implementation closures on the private direct-call path. |\n56:| **HIGH** | [yang.preludes.md:379](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:379), [line 466](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:466) | `:raw-or-call` carries an executable `:overflow-op`. The exact-export and reserved-door checks enumerate `:hooks` and `:ambient-projections`, leaving this literal-strategy target outside the stated checks. Finding an export somewhere in `artifact-store` also does not establish that the selected runtime closure authorizes it for that position. | Validate every descriptor field that can emit a call against the selected, address-verified closure and its frontend-authorized role. Apply qualification, arity, and reserved-door rules to literal strategies as well as hooks and projections. |\n57:| **MEDIUM** | [yang.preludes.md:302](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:302) | The proposed validator promises to check numeric floors from the registry. Host registration publishes export profiles and functions. `integer/max-bits` is absent from the export inventory, and the existing Python registrar checks the explicit limits map before constructing the registry. [Host registration](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:249) · [Integer exports](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/integer.cljc:592) · [Python registration](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:4163) | Pass the trusted composition limits into admission or retain verifiable limit declarations at registration. Distinguish the root’s direct `:requires` pins from the transitively verified closure so a nested dependency need not be declared as a direct edge. |\n60:| **LOW** | [yang.preludes.md:283](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:283) | The active `nil` ceiling works. The adjacent four-effect example omits at least `:cell/new-provenance` and `:cell/provenance`, both used by the Python runtime. [Python host dependencies](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:204) · [Declared effects](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:446) | Remove the illustrative set or derive a sufficient example from the verified Python closure. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
