{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc | sed -n '116,161p;331,354p'\"","aggregated_output":"   116\t(defn resolve-var\n   117\t  \"Look up a variable name: env -> store -> primitives -> module registry.\n   118\t\n   119\t   A reserved name (Rule R: `yin/def` is syntax, never a name) is refused\n   120\t   before env or store is consulted, so no binding, store entry, or\n   121\t   registry can give it a meaning. Every executing variable lookup of\n   122\t   every engine goes through here.\n   123\t\n   124\t   The registry is a value supplied by the composition, not a global.\"\n   125\t  [env store primitives registry name]\n   126\t  (when (vm/reserved-name? name)\n   127\t    (vm/refuse-reserved! :variable name))\n   128\t  (if-let [pair (find env name)]\n   129\t    (val pair)\n   130\t    (if-let [pair (find store name)]\n   131\t      (val pair)\n   132\t      (if-let [pair (find primitives name)]\n   133\t        (vm/primitive-function (val pair))\n   134\t        (if-let [resolved (when (namespace name)\n   135\t                            (module/resolve-module\n   136\t                              registry\n   137\t                              (symbol (str (namespace name)\n   138\t                                           \".\"\n   139\t                                           (clojure.core/name name)))))]\n   140\t          resolved\n   141\t          (fail (str \"Unable to resolve symbol: \" name \" in this context\")\n   142\t                {:symbol name}))))))\n   143\t\n   144\t\n   145\t(defn check-store-key!\n   146\t  \"Refuse a program store access whose key is a reserved name (Rule R):\n   147\t   the definition operator is never a store key.\"\n   148\t  [key]\n   149\t  (when (vm/reserved-name? key)\n   150\t    (vm/refuse-reserved! :store-key key)))\n   151\t\n   152\t\n   153\t(defn store-put\n   154\t  \"The one program store write: every definition transition, the\n   155\t   `:vm/store-put` effect, and the four direct store instructions write\n   156\t   through here, and a reserved key is refused. Every other store write\n   157\t   `yin.vm.store-write-audit-test` detects is state construction on its\n   158\t   allowlist; that namespace states what it detects and the residual it\n   159\t   leaves to review.\"\n   160\t  [store key val]\n   161\t  (check-store-key! key)\n   331\t\n   332\t(defn authentic-ref?\n   333\t  \"True when `ref` is a `kind` reference this task issued: its seal\n   334\t   verifies under the task's secret, and it names a live resource of that\n   335\t   kind. A `:cell-ref` is checked against `:heap` instead: its id is live\n   336\t   by `contains?` (a cell may hold nil) and its seal equals the one the\n   337\t   heap entry recorded at allocation, so no hash is computed per access.\"\n   338\t  [state kind ref]\n   339\t  (let [secret (:capability-secret state)\n   340\t        id (when (map? ref) (:id ref))]\n   341\t    (if (= :cell-ref kind)\n   342\t      (let [heap (:heap state)]\n   343\t        (boolean (and (some? secret)\n   344\t                      (= kind (:type ref))\n   345\t                      (contains? heap id)\n   346\t                      (= (:seal ref) (:seal (get heap id))))))\n   347\t      (let [resource (get (:resources state) id)]\n   348\t        (boolean (and (some? secret)\n   349\t                      (= kind (:type ref))\n   350\t                      (some? resource)\n   351\t                      (= (:seal ref) (seal-of secret kind id))\n   352\t                      (= (= :cursor-ref kind) (cursor-cell? resource))))))))\n   353\t\n   354\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
