{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'float-floor|clj.py/eq|sequential\\\\?|reduced\\\\?|clj.py/.*export|\\\\byin/def\\\\b' docs/design/yang.preludes.md | tail -45\"","aggregated_output":"46:1. **Duplicated guest runtime mechanics:** ~1,200–2,000 lines of guest UAST across `py`, `js`, `php`, and `clj` implement the same core algorithms under language-prefixed names: `%capture` handler stacks, IEEE-754 float64 math (`fmod-pos` Sterbenz loop, integer-exponent squaring with split-half reciprocal `neg-power`, `nan`/`inf`/`-0.0`, `float-floor` binary descent, `float-parts`, decimal layout over `integer/float-digits`), fixed-width integer wrapping and radix digit scanning, `gen-switch` coroutine stepping, and `stream/poll!` signal safepoint hooks.\n81:   - **No descriptor hook or source-facing ambient projection** may expose `cell/dsg__*`, `dsg__*`, `yin/def`, `*.rt/*`, `*.b/*`, `yang.safepoint/*`, or non-projectable internal adapter entries such as `clojure.core/raw-*` (`§6.3`).\n190:   - Every cross-boundary numeric function that can encounter an exceptional edge condition (`neg-pow-result`, `floor-int-result`) takes a **boxed `data/float64` input** and returns either a **boxed `data/float64` / exact integer** OR a **pure status keyword** (`:yrt.float/underflow`, `:yrt.float/out-of-range`) **after** exiting the leaf frame. Outer Layer-2b wrappers (`py`, `js`, `php`, `clj.py`) inspect the returned status keyword safely outside any raw-double stack frame and only then raise language-specific exceptions or compute signed `±Inf` from the boxed input and exact exponent. Total IEEE float-floor (`float-floor-raw` / `float-floor`, matching `yang.python.antlr.prelude:1441`) needs no status keyword because `|x| >= 2^53`, `±Inf`, and `NaN` are already integral or pass through unchanged.\n209:| `float-floor-raw`, `float-floor` | `float-floor-raw [x]` (leaf raw); `float-floor [x-boxed]` (boxed) | Total IEEE double floor: binary descent + `data/float-value` for finite `|x| < 2^53`, returning `x` unchanged for `|x| >= 2^53`, `±Inf`, `NaN`; zero callbacks |\n400:  :op/eq            'clj.py/eq\n489:     - **Reserved-door ban:** Refuses any descriptor whose `:hooks`, executable `:literals.*` fields, or `:ambient-projections` references `cell/dsg__*`, `dsg__*`, `yin/def`, `*.rt/*`, `*.b/*`, `yang.safepoint/*`, or non-projectable internal adapter entries (`clojure.core/raw-*`), or exposes any unprivileged raw primitive without projection. Registry availability never grants source-level authority.\n535:| Equality `==` / `!=` | `1 == 1.0 == True`, structural list/dict | Recursive kind-strict equality (`clj.py/eq`): `1 == 1` `true`, `1 == 1.0` `false`, `1 == True` `false`, `NaN == NaN` `false`, `0.0 == -0.0` `true`, recursive over persistent collections |\n568:   - **`//` (`clj.py/float-floordiv`):**\n572:     - Finite `x`, finite nonzero `y`: inside pure leaf helper `clj.py/float-floordiv-raw [x y]`, mirrors `py/float-divmod` (`src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:1427–1437`):\n577:       - **Quotient rounding correction:** `(let [f (yrt.float/float-floor-raw div)] (if (< (data/float-value 0.5) (- div f)) (+ f (data/float-value 1)) f))` — ensures `2.1 // 0.7` (whose intermediate `div` is `2.9999999999999996`, flooring to `2.0`) evaluates to **`3.0`** while non-finite or `>= 2^53` quotients pass through unchanged; result is boxed via `data/float64`.\n590:4. **Uniform portable key/element domain (`admit-key!`) & recursive equality (`clj.py/eq`, `clj.py/ne`):**\n597:   - **Recursive portable equality (`clj.py/eq`, `clj.py/ne`):** Never delegates floats or float-bearing values to host `=`, because CLJS `Float64.-equiv` (`src/cljc/dao/host/number.cljc:98–101`) equates `NaN` with `NaN` and distinguishes `-0.0` from `0.0`:\n601:     - Vectors / sequential collections (`data/vector?`, `clojure.core/sequential?`): equal count + pairwise recursive `clj.py/eq`.\n602:     - Maps (`data/map?`,