{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'owned|:yang.semantics/ambient-modules|host-limits|provenance' docs/design/yang.preludes.md | head -58\"","aggregated_output":"62:   - Lowering preserves source CST identity; compiled UAST roots under different preludes have distinct content addresses (or identical addresses when two descriptors emit identical UAST) linked by explicit provenance datoms pinning `(cst-address, lowering-profile, semantics-descriptor, runtime-profile, unit-address)`.\n79:8. **Security boundary — VM provenance doors stay private:** Under `src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md` and `src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc`, `cell/dsg__new-provenance` and `cell/dsg__provenance` are reserved compiler/runtime-module doors whose names guest code must not forge or re-export.\n80:   - **`yrt.*` modules, `clj.py`, and Layer-2c standard libraries (such as `clojure.core`) MUST NEVER wrap, mint, read, declare, or export provenance-door primitives or `:cell/new-provenance` / `:cell/provenance` effects.**\n82:   - Retained protocol-condition provenance (`yang.antlr.md` §8.10.7) resides strictly inside trusted Layer-2b runtime modules (`py`, `js`, `php`, `clj`, and **`clj.bridge`**) in **both** bundled (`uast`) and linked (`module-uast`) emission, never exported and never exposed across `yrt.*`, Layer-2c libraries, or source scope.\n124:| **Provenance doors** | `cell/dsg__new-provenance` and `cell/dsg__provenance` are security-sensitive VM doors (`§2.2` invariant 8). |\n232:  - **Context policy difference (`py` vs. `php`):** In live code, `py/gen-enter` (`yang.python.antlr.prelude:457–458`) and `py/gen-start` (`:470`) compute a rebased `:base = (+ 1 (abs-depth caller-ctx))`, whereas `php/gen-start` (`yang.php.antlr.prelude:5311`) starts at `(php/ctx nil 0 0 nil)` and `php/gen-enter` (`:5305`) restores `(get s :ctx)` directly without rebasing. `yrt.gen` therefore accepts explicit `on-start-ctx` and `on-resume-ctx` policy closures alongside `on-enter`, `on-exit`, `on-fail`, and `on-throw-closed`, keeping PHP's refcount/cleanup lifecycle (`cleanup`, `addref`/`release`) and Python's `RecursionError` admission checks strictly language-owned.\n286:    :yang.prelude/max-effects nil} ;; optional allowed-effect ceiling (e.g., the verified Python closure's #{:cell/new :cell/get :cell/set! :cell/authentic? :cell/new-provenance :cell/provenance}); nil = derive from verified closure without an extra ceiling\n303:   - Validation verifies that no `yrt.*`, `clj.py`, or Layer-2c (e.g., `clojure.core`) manifest in the closure exports any `dsg__*` symbol or declares `:cell/new-provenance` or `:cell/provenance` in its derived effects.\n307:   - Because `yin.vm.module/register-host-module` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:249`) stores exports and profiles without retaining raw limit declarations (`yin.vm.integer` does not export `integer/max-bits`, and `yang.python.antlr.prelude/register-integer-module:4163` validates an explicit `limits` map before registration), **`admit-profile` takes `(profile artifact-store registry host-limits)`**.\n308:   - Verifies that `registry` supplies every required host export (`prelude-admission/admit`) AND verifies every declared floor in `:yang.prelude/host-modules` (`:min-bits`, `:min-digits`, `:min-max-items`) against the trusted composition `host-limits` map (failing closed if `host-limits` is absent or below the required floor, and cross-checking `integer/max-digits` / `data/max-items` against `host-limits` when present).\n325:Level 2 strictly subsumes Level 1: a semantics descriptor defines **both** what lowering emits for syntax constructs (`:yang.semantics/hooks` + `:yang.semantics/literals`) and which ambient modules/identifiers enter source scope (`:yang.semantics/ambient-modules` + `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections`).\n349: :yang.semantics/ambient-modules\n485:     - Computes the descriptor's **selected, address-verified closure**: every `[module address]` in `:yang.semantics/ambient-modules` must resolve in `artifact-store` along with its full transitive `:requires` DAG (with unique module-symbol bindings).\n506:### 6.5 Frontend SPI and provenance integration (`yang.frontend`)\n512:- Compilation provenance records `(cst-address, lowering-profile, runtime-profile, unit-address)` as data; note that distinct descriptors may legitimately yield identical UAST addresses on simple programs (many-to-one), so provenance retains the exact compilation tuple rather than inferring the descriptor from the UAST address alone.\n616:| `:fn/call` | `[callee args]` | Delegates directly to trusted Layer-2b **`clj.bridge/invoke-callable`** (`§7.4`), which checks `clj.bridge/admitted-callable?` first and routes to `yang.call/invoke` with the condition-unwrapping / provenance-retaining raise exit. Zero provenance doors inside `clj.py`. |\n633:**Trusted Layer-2b provenance boundary (`clj.bridge`):**\n634:All Clojure-family §8.10.7 entry/call provenance bridging is consolidated into a **single stateless trusted Layer-2b module `clj.bridge`** (`src/cljc/yang/clojure/bridge.cljc`), requiring `yang.call`, `yrt.escape`, and `clj`.\n635:- `clj.bridge` owns the private provenance doors (`cell/dsg__new-provenance`, `cell/dsg__provenance`) inside **both** its linked (`module-uast`) and bundled (`uast`) emitters (preserving §5.2 Bundled vs. Linked Parity Law!), never exporting them and keeping them strictly out of `yrt.*`, `clj.py`, and Layer-2c `clojure.core`.\n653:   - Any plain source map (including `{:yang.call/entry ...}`), unauthenticated `{:type :cell-ref ...}` map, or raw host primitive/continuation fails `admitted-callable?` cleanly; `invoke-callable` mints a retained `:yang.call/not-callable` protocol condition via private `cell/dsg__new-provenance` and raises it via `(clj/raise ...)`, never calling `yang.call/invoke` on forged source data.\n664:     - On escape with `e`, the handler inspects private `(cell/dsg__provenance e)`: if non-nil (an authentic retained protocol condition from a deeper cross-language boundary), forwards that retained condition **directly** to `raise-exit` without double-wrapping; otherwise wraps `e` (including condition-shaped user maps!) via `(yang.call/thrown e)` and transfers it to `raise-exit`.\n666:   - Validates `(clj.bridge/admitted-callable? callee)`; if false, mints private retained `:yang.call/not-callable` via `cell/dsg__new-provenance` and raises on `(clj/rt-ctx)`.\n669:     - Otherwise retains the protocol condition inside a private provenance carrier `(clj/raise (cell/dsg__new-provenance condition condition))` (mirroring `clojure.cljc:1448–1450`), preserving full condition fidelity across `A → B → A` unwinds and `finally` blocks, as well as nested `clj → clj.py → clj` unwinding on `(clj/rt-ctx)`.\n673:In Slice P3, `clojure.core` is published as an **explicit, standalone, portable Layer-2c linker module** (`clojure.core`) requiring `yang.call`, `clj`, `clj.bridge`, `yrt.float`, and `yrt.int` (zero direct provenance doors!), and registered against host modules `kind` (with pure `kind/namespace`), `data` (with pure `data/float64?`), `integer` (`:min-bits 53`), and `cell` (strictly omitting host-dependent exports):\n764:| **P0 — Composition plumbing & `defquoted` consolidation** | Consolidate `defquoted` into `yang.core.prelude`; implement `:yang.prelude/recipe` / `:yang.prelude/profile` composition, `validate-profile`, and `admit-profile` (with explicit `host-limits`, direct-root vs. transitive closure separation, operand sequencing, `init!` placement, tail marking, `:linear`/`:balanced` mode, and Clojure's custom preamble). | **Zero** (byte-identical emission) | Compare generated UAST/specs against frozen pre-change snapshots of `py`/`js`/`php`/`clj`/`yang.call`; test direct-vs.-transitive `:requires` closure validation (including transitive-only dependencies), missing transitive artifact/export refusal, `host-limits` numeric-floor enforcement, provenance-door/effect-ceiling exclusions, and projected-name collision refusal. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
