{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md | sed -n '244,286p'\"","aggregated_output":"   244\tBoring collection or record mappings are admitted. All lengths and integer\n   245\targuments use shortest definite encodings; integers fitting CBOR major\n   246\ttypes 0/1 do not use bignum tags, and bignum magnitudes have no leading zero.\n   247\t\n   248\t### Ingress limits and host-capability refusals\n   249\t\n   250\tRatified from the J0-J3 fixture corpus and its errata\n   251\t(`test/resources/dao/jing/cbor-v1.errata.md`), not derived from the text\n   252\tabove: an implementation must enforce these explicitly rather than rely on\n   253\thost defaults.\n   254\t\n   255\t- Cap CBOR item nesting depth at 128 on both encode and decode, counting the\n   256\t  top-level item as depth 1 and every array, map, and tag as one level\n   257\t  deeper (a `dao.jing/list` frame therefore costs three levels). Refuse\n   258\t  `:unsupported-value` on encode and `:malformed-cbor` on decode past the\n   259\t  cap; this is a robustness rule against unbounded recursion, independent\n   260\t  of the profile's other refusal classes.\n   261\t- Constrain a decimal's exponent to `[-(2^31 - 1), 2^31]`, the JVM\n   262\t  `BigDecimal` scale range, identically on every host. Refuse\n   263\t  `:malformed-number` outside it. Without a shared window, one host can\n   264\t  accept a canonical payload another host refuses, letting the accepting\n   265\t  host determine the boundary the contract otherwise forbids.\n   266\t- A host whose identifier equality is joined-name-based (ClojureScript\n   267\t  keywords and symbols compare by namespace/name joined into one string)\n   268\t  cannot hold two Jing values that are namespace/name-distinct but\n   269\t  joined-name-equal (for example `(keyword nil \"a/b\")` and\n   270\t  `(keyword \"a\" \"b\")`) in one decoded map or set without merging them. This\n   271\t  is a host materialization limit, not a Jing acceptance rule: portable\n   272\t  equality (`equiv`) keeps such values distinct, and the encoded bytes are\n   273\t  canonical and unambiguous. Refuse with `:host-collapse`, a class outside\n   274\t  the sixteen decode-refusal classes above, on a host that cannot hold the\n   275\t  value. `:host-collapse` is a per-host capability refusal: J3's cross-host\n   276\t  conformance requires identical outcomes across hosts except this named\n   277\t  class, applied only on hosts whose identifier equality actually merges.\n   278\t\n   279\t### Numeric identity\n   280\t\n   281\tPreserve integer, floating-point, decimal, and rational kinds. This is an\n   282\texplicit user choice: an integer `1` and floating-point `1.0` have different\n   283\taddresses. Host integer width is not identity; small and big integers of the\n   284\tsame value share an address.\n   285\t\n   286\tCarriers must implement portable `=`/`hash`/`compare` consistently across\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
