{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.antlr.md | sed -n '3597,3612p;3685,3699p;3946,3962p'\"","aggregated_output":"  3597\tThis is an obligation of construction and source resolution, not a new\n  3598\tVM type, descriptor seal, or runtime provenance/language registry. Once\n  3599\tthe resolved descriptor is admitted, the shared projection is structural;\n  3600\tUAST deliberately constructing a conforming descriptor opts into the\n  3601\tconvention rather than changing a source language's data-map semantics.\n  3602\t\n  3603\tMissing entry means not callable. Constructors must install a genuine\n  3604\tunary Yin closure, and supported source mutations must preserve that\n  3605\tinvariant. Unary arity is a constructor/profile conformance obligation,\n  3606\tnot a signature introspection operation: Yin closures are opaque and the\n  3607\tVM's existing argument binding does not enforce this convention's arity.\n  3608\tA key in a map grants no VM privilege; application, ownership, and\n  3609\teffect checks still apply. A non-applicable entry remains an operational\n  3610\tVM application defect, not a source exception caught by the shared helper.\n  3611\t\n  3612\tFor callable kinds whose eligibility can change, the same cell or\n  3685\tAn absent receiver differs from one whose value is `nil`, `:py/None`,\n  3686\t`:php/null`, `:js/null`, or `:js/undefined`. Empty argument vectors are\n  3687\trequired rather than represented by absent keys. Presence must not be\n  3688\tinferred from truthiness.\n  3689\t\n  3690\tThe optional binding profile pins additional argument semantics. It\n  3691\tdoes not name the caller's language or select a language-pair bridge.\n  3692\tAbsent that extension, arguments are by-value runtime values as in\n  3693\tsection 8.10.6. The callee entry compares the supplied profile address\n  3694\twith its declared accepted/required binding profiles before acquiring\n  3695\treferences or entering the body. An unsupported required profile or a\n  3696\tmissing required extension fails there. The pinned profile defines the\n  3697\tshape and validation of any extra invocation fields it requires; values\n  3698\tin the base vectors alone do not establish a location protocol.\n  3699\t\n  3946\t#### 8.10.9 Publication, visibility, and reproducibility\n  3947\t\n  3948\tShared callability creates no common global scope. An import or\n  3949\tcomposition explicitly binds exports in the receiving source namespace\n  3950\tunder its normal name/module rules. Missing names keep their source\n  3951\terrors. No fallback searches other frontends, the filesystem, a host\n  3952\tpackage registry, or ambient globals.\n  3953\t\n  3954\tLinked modules publish code and immutable specifications. Their bodies\n  3955\tinstantiate function objects and common entries in the importing task,\n  3956\tas section 8.5.6 requires. Install children must not export live function\n  3957\tcells. A higher-order result is an ordinary runtime value, not a new\n  3958\tlinker publication on each call.\n  3959\t\n  3960\tLowering/runtime profiles pin the implementation and binding/value\n  3961\textensions. Existing dependency/effect/custody checks remain. Type facts\n  3962\tstay beside code under `yin.vm.typecheck`, not in lambda language tags.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'dsg__add|<=|unwind-to|nil\\\\? hs|abandon-to' docs/design/yang.preludes.md | head -24\"","aggregated_output":"141:Reconciles the current per-language divergences (`4-slot` vs `5-slot` frames, `:base` rebasing, `:generator` boundary frames, `orelse` vs value-return, PHP `abandon-to`, normal-exit `finally` sentinel, and empty-stack handling) by parameterizing `ctx-cell`, `normal-arg`, and `on-empty`:\n149:    - **`n` (slot 3):** monotonic handler-stack frame count `(+ 1 (frame-depth rest))` used strictly by `unwind-to` and `abandon-to` for O(1) structural depth comparison (`<= (data/nth hs 3) n`).\n165:| `unwind-to` | `[ctx-cell n normal-arg]` | Pop frames while `(> (data/nth hs 3) n)`, running each `:finally` thunk with `normal-arg` (`:py/None`, `:js/undefined`, `:php/null`, `nil`) |\n166:| `abandon-to` | `[ctx-cell n]` | Pop frames while `(> (data/nth hs 3) n)` **without** running `:finally` thunks (PHP terminal fatals / `exit`) |\n170:| `call-ec` | `[ctx-cell f normal-arg]` | Capture escape continuation that runs `unwind-to` then `restore!` before invoking `r` |\n171:| `call-terminal` | `[ctx-cell f]` | Capture terminal escape that runs `abandon-to` then `restore!` before invoking `r` (`php`) |\n174:- In `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2470–2517`, the live preamble currently constructs **four** portable guest helpers (`dsg__get`, `dsg__equal`, `dsg__assoc`, `dsg__empty`), while `conj` and `vec` are protected against local shadowing by the convention's binder checks (`clojure.cljc:2479`), and `+` / `<=` currently have no `dsg__*` helpers. Note that `dsg__get` (`clojure.cljc:2484–2497`) scans only maps (`data/map?`) and returns `nil` on vectors.\n176:- Thus, when `yrt.escape/uast` is bundled inline into non-linked `yang.clojure`, it reads `get`, `=`, `assoc`, `conj`, `+`, and `<=` as follows without breaking UCF machine-data validation (never binding host primitive functions inside guest environments):\n179:  - `+` and `<=` are wrapped by adding two portable guest closures `dsg__add` and `dsg__lte` (using `(+ a b)` / `(<= a b)` when unshadowed, and safe binary integer arithmetic or binder-check refusal when `+` or `<=` is defined in `(::defined env)` — all pure guest lambdas, matching `dsg__get` at `clojure.cljc:2484`).\n203:| `nan?`, `finite?`, `zero?`, `neg-zero?`, `abs`, `neg`, `zero-like` | Unwrapped host double `x` inside leaf frames (`zero-like` takes `[y]`); no `%capture`/safepoints | Pure leaf boolean or unwrapped double (`nan?`: `(not (<= x x))`; `finite?`: `(< (abs x) (data/float-value ##Inf))`; `zero-like`: `copysign(0.0, y)`) |\n541:Per `yang.antlr.md` §8.5.5, raw `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=` on decoded `data/float64` carriers are **not portable across Node/JVM/Dart**. Furthermore, `yin.vm.data/data-number?` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc:418`) recognizes host numbers and exact-integer carriers, **not** CLJS `Float64` carriers (`src/cljc/dao/host/number.cljc:76`).\n559:   - `+`, `-`, `*`, `//`, `%`, `**` (`e >= 0`), `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`: check `b == 0` **before** `integer/floor-div-mod` or `integer/true-div` (raising guest zero-division error rather than an operational throw); filter `floor-div-mod` through `yrt.int/check-limit` before calling `data/nth` for `//` or `%`.\n589:   - **Mixed ordering (`<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`):** Float × Float unwraps both via `data/float-value` inside a pure leaf helper; Int × Float / Float × Int unwraps the boxed float via `data/float-value` inside a pure leaf helper, returns `false` if `(yrt.float/nan? f)`, and calls `integer/compare-float` strictly on the unwrapped non-NaN host double (never passing a boxed CLJS `Float64` or `NaN` to `integer/compare-float` and never rounding large integers to float).\n765:| **P1 — Layer 2a Tier 1 (`yrt.escape`, `yrt.float`, `yrt.int`)** | Implement the three stateless guest modules (frame indexing via `data/nth`, status-returning `yrt.float` boxed boundaries `neg-pow-result` / `floor-int-result` plus total `float-floor-raw` with zero raw-double callbacks and no `data/float64?` dependency); migrate `js`/`clj` from 4-slot to 5-slot contexts (`:handlers :depth :base :frame`); preserve open non-`:finally` (`:generator`) boundary dispatch; add `dsg__add`/`dsg__lte` guest helpers for bundled `clj`; activate across `py`, `js`, `php`, `clj` in one coordinated bump. | **One batched bump** | Unit tests for `yrt.*` on semantic/stack/register VMs; bundled/linked `yang.clojure` parity with source-defined `(defn get ...)` and active nested `try`/`throw`/`finally` frames; existing Python & PHP generator tests green; 4→5-slot migration tests; PHP `abandon-to` / `call-terminal` & normal `finally` replacement (`:py/None`, `:js/undefined`, `:php/null`, `nil`); `1.1 ** 6` bit-pattern parity (`fpow-half-raw` vs `fpow-base-raw`); exceptional `yrt.float` underflow (`0.5 ** -2000` -> `:yrt.float/underflow` + outer overflow policy), subnormal (`2.0 ** -1074` -> `5e-324`), normal zero (`2.0 ** -2000` -> `+0.0`), and out-of-range (`floor(1e30)`, `floor(NaN)`, `floor(Inf)`) witnesses under `%capture`/safepoints across 4 hosts; `yin.vm.integer` v4 three-reason translation without masking operational throws; independent concurrent `py`/`js`/`php`/`clj` tasks sharing `yrt.*`; bundled == linked + 4-host + CPython/Node/PHP oracle parity; `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj` clean. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
