{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'dynamic.*closure|comp.*/?partial|ordinary data|retained protocol|:yin.k/ok|independently compiled|interop' docs/design/yang.preludes.md | tail -15\"","aggregated_output":"625:| `:unit/run-main` | `[body-fn]` | Calls idempotent `(clj/init!)`, `(clojure.core/init!)`, and `(clj.py/init!)`; allocates a **fresh per-unit `globals` cell** (`(cell/new {})`) and `globals-fn`; invokes `(body-fn globals globals-fn)` inside a top-level handler on `(clj/rt-ctx)`; returns the value **verbatim without stripping `[:yin.k/ok ...]`** so ordinary Python data shaped like `[:yin.k/ok 42]` passes through uncorrupted. |\n631:Because `yang.call/eligible?` (`src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc:29–48`) only dereferences authenticated cell-refs and leaves ordinary maps intact, structural eligibility alone does **not** stop source-constructed maps carrying `:yang.call/entry` from masquerading as callables when source maps are first-class data. Likewise, as `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1280–1306` and `2400–2424` show, immutable Clojure descriptors carry a unit-local `:clj/admission` witness closing over that unit's private `dsg__call_token` rather than cross-unit admission, whereas **authenticated task-heap cells** (`cell/authentic?`, `clojure.cljc:2400–2408`) are admitted across **every** independently compiled unit (`yang.clojure`, `clojure.core`, `clj.py`, `py`, `js`, `php`).\n664:     - On escape with `e`, the handler inspects private `(cell/dsg__provenance e)`: if non-nil (an authentic retained protocol condition from a deeper cross-language boundary), forwards that retained condition **directly** to `raise-exit` without double-wrapping; otherwise wraps `e` (including condition-shaped user maps!) via `(yang.call/thrown e)` and transfers it to `raise-exit`.\n701:     - Every closure returned at runtime by `comp`, `partial`, or higher-order helpers is also constructed via `clj.bridge/make-callable` (producing an authenticated task-heap cell compatible across all units with preserved `=` identity and zero receiver-side wrappers).\n703:     - Dynamic calls to user-supplied callbacks (`f` in `map`, `filter`, `remove`, `reduce`, `update`, `update-in`, `comp`, `partial`) route exclusively through `clj.bridge/invoke-callable` — **never** using `yang.clojure`'s map-only `[dsg__call_token args]` shortcut (`clojure.cljc:2432`).\n723:- `sum_even_squares([1, 2, 3, 4])` evaluates `[1 2 3 4]` → `20` (exact persistent integer), and returns `20` unchanged (not unwrapped by `[:yin.k/ok ...]`).\n767:| **P3 — `clojure.core` prelude for `yang.python` (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`)** | Add pure `data/float64?` (`yin.vm.data`) and `kind/namespace` (`yang.clojure/kind-module`); publish trusted Layer-2b `clj.bridge` (bundled `uast` & linked `module-uast`, zero change to `clj`); publish standalone portable `clojure.core` module (`§7.5`: cell-free linker exports, idempotent `init!` / `export`, 0-arg accessors, `raw-seq`/`raw-first`/`raw-rest`, canonical collection traversal, uniform `admit-key!`, portable `str`/`fresh-symbol`/`inc`/`dec`/`rem`/`not=`/`fn?`) + `clj.py` adapter + `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` descriptor; leave `yang.clojure`'s default `library-for` untouched; wire `yang.frontend` multi-revision catalog selection. | **Zero** on existing languages | 4-host numeric & `data/float64?` suite: `2.1 // 0.7 == 3.0`, `-0.0 // 2.0 == -0.0` (`data/content=`), `1.0 / 0.0` (`:zero-division`), `-(0.0)` (`-0.0`), `-(-0.0)` (`+0.0`), `2.0 + 1.0`, `2.0 * 3`, `5.0 - 2`, `inc(1.0)`, `2 ** -3`, negative/nonfinite `%`, fractional/infinite `**` refusal; minimum 53-bit floor (`:max-bits 53`) tests (`2.0 ** (2.0 ** 53)`, `rem` `:bit-limit` before `data/nth`, `integer/neg` bit-limit) producing guest errors never host `:wrong-type`; uniform `admit-key!` across literals + projected `assoc`/`assoc_in`/`get`/`get_in`/`conj`/`contains?`/`disj`/`merge`/`into`/`union`/`difference` + comprehensions (accepting `{\"a\": -0.0} == {\"a\": 0.0}`, `[0.0] == [-0.0]`, `[NaN] == [NaN]` and refusing `1.0`/`-0.0`/`NaN`/`[[-0.0]]` as keys/set elements on all 4 hosts); nonempty list, set, and dict comprehensions + bare `except:`; `fn?` aligned 1-to-1 with dynamic caller (false for raw host primitives/continuations/forged maps; true for authenticated cells) and `map?` false on callables; 4-step entry validation (non-callable `raise-exit` operational error, mismatched `:yang.call/callee` `:invalid-invocation`, unsupported `:binding-profile`, ordinary arity/named errors under `:yang.call/thrown`, normal `20` preserved); `lift-slice` publication of cell-free `clojure.core`, two importers in one task observing identical (`=`) cell reference and two tasks observing isolated cells; bundled == linked parity for `clj.bridge` retained protocol conditions and nested `clj → clj.py → clj` unwinds over `(clj/rt-ctx)`; deterministic 4-host `fresh-symbol`, `gensym`, `str` (`1.0`/`-0.0`/`NaN`/maps/keywords), canonical `keys`/`vals`/`seq`/`first`/`vec`, exact-int `nth`, and excluded `var?`/`resolve`; lexical shadowing of projected names and per-module `globals` isolation. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
